4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Repeating the measurement a number of times and averaging the results reduces the effect of random uncertainty.,"Repeating,measurement,number,times,averaging,results,reduces,effect,random,uncertainty"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Usually，only one significant figure should be kept.,"Usually,one,significant,figure,kept"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Percentage uncertainty: The percentage uncertainty changes with the amount of material that you are measuring. Percentage uncertainty is also a guiding factor in choosing equipment for an experiment.,"Percentage,uncertainty,percentage,uncertainty,changes,amount,material,measuring,Percentage,uncertainty,also,guiding,factor,choosing,equipment,experiment"
