4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,7.1 Development of Periodic Table,"Development,Periodic,Table"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"1790s: Antoine Lavoisier compiled a list of 23 elements known at the time; by 1870, there were approximately 70 known elements","Antoine,Lavoisier,compiled,list,elements,known,time,approximately,known,elements"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,1860s: Chemists developed and agreed upon a method of determining the atomic mass of elements,"Chemists,developed,agreed,upon,method,determining,atomic,mass,elements"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,1864: John Newlands observed the repetition of properties in every eight elements. This demonstrates a periodic change because it repeats a specific manner.,"John,Newlands,observed,repetition,properties,every,eight,elements,demonstrates,periodic,change,repeats,specific,manner"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,1869: Dmitri Mendeleev and Lothar Meyer both demonstrated connection between atomic mass and elemental properties. Mendeleev was given more credit because he was the earliest one to publish his organization plan and demonstrated how it was useful,"Dmitri,Mendeleev,Lothar,Meyer,demonstrated,connection,atomic,mass,elemental,properties,Mendeleev,given,credit,earliest,one,publish,organization,plan,demonstrated,useful"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Mendeleev noticed that when the elements were ordered by increasing atomic mass, there was a repetition, or periodic pattern, in their chemical and physical properties.","Mendeleev,noticed,elements,ordered,increasing,atomic,mass,repetition,periodic,pattern,chemical,physical,properties"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,He showed that the properties of the elements repeat in an orderly way from row to row of the table.,"showed,properties,elements,repeat,orderly,way,row,row,table"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Elements in vertical columns showed similar properties.,"Elements,vertical,columns,showed,similar,properties"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Mendeleev correctly predicted the existence and properties of undiscovered elements.,"Mendeleev,correctly,predicted,existence,properties,undiscovered,elements"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In order to group elements with similar properties in the same columns, Mendeleev had to leave some blank spaces in his table.","order,group,elements,similar,properties,columns,Mendeleev,leave,blank,spaces,table"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"By noting the trends in the properties of known elements, he was able to predict the properties of the yet-to-be discovered elements scandium, gallium, and germanium (which he called eka-silicon）.","noting,trends,properties,known,elements,able,predict,properties,yet,discovered,elements,scandium,gallium,germanium,called,eka,silicon"
4 IDX G9 CHEM S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1913, Henry Moseley’s arrangement of elements by atomic number resulted in a clear periodic pattern of properties.","Henry,Moseley,arrangement,elements,atomic,number,resulted,clear,periodic,pattern,properties"
