Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"12.1 Iden)fying The Substance of Genes Role of DNA ●Storing informaCon(The geneCc material stores informaCon needed by every living cell(Ion transport, movement, cell growth, respiraCon) ●Copying informaCon -> before a call divides, its geneCc informaCon must be copied ●TransmiWng i n f o r m aCon -> when a cell divides, each daughter cell must get a complete copy of geneCc informaCon  Experimental Proof of DNA as GeneCc Material Frederick Griﬃth’s Experiments on Bacterial TransformaCon  ●2 diﬀerent pneumonia bacterial stains -> test of mice ■Smooth Strain (S Strain) -> disease causing, grow into smooth colonies ■Rough Strain (R Strain) -> harmless, grow into colonies with rough edges  1.Disease-causing bacteria (S Strain) -> inject in mouse -> mouse dies of pneumonia  2.Harmless bacteria (R Strain) -> inject in mouse -> mouse lives  3.Heat killed S Strain bacteria -> inject in mouse -> mouse lives  ●Conclusion: cause of pneumonia was not a toxin from these disease-causing bacteria 4.Mixture of heat killed S Strain and living R Strain -> inject in mouse -> mouse dies of pneumonia -> live, disease-causing bacteria in the mouse’s blood (S Strain) was found  ●TransformaCon: process where one strain of bacteria is changed permanently by a gene or genes of another strain of bacteria  Oswald Avery’s Experiment to Discover the Molecular Cause of TransformaCon ●Remove lipids, carbohydrates, protein, RNA, DNA from a soluCon of heat killed S Strain  1.Add enzymes that remove RNA (ribonuclease), lipids, carbohydrates, protein (proteinase) -> no RNA, lipids, carbohydrates, protein lec in sample -> add R Strain into sample -> transformaCon occurs  2.Add enzyme to remove DNA (deoxyribonuclease) -> no DNA lec in sample -> add R Strain into sample -> S Strain doesn’t appear  ●Conclusion: DNA is the molecule that stores and transmits geneCc informaCon from oner generaCon of an organism to the next","Iden,fying,Substance,Genes,Role,DNA,Storing,in