Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"■Viruses that infect bacteria  ■Consists of protein coat and DNA/RNA core  ■How they aﬀect bacteria -> bacteriophage latch onto bacteria -> bacteriophage DNA injected into cell, taking over bacteria’s funcCons -> host bacteria begin producing new virus parts -> viruses are assembled, ﬁlling the bacteria -> bacteria explode and releases new viruses  ●Used radioacCve markers (isotopes) for experiment  ■35S(Sulfur) only mark on protein  ■32P(Phosphorus) only mark on DNA  1.35S on protein coat of virus -> bacteriophages infect bacteria with geneCc material -> no radioacCvity enters  2.32P mark on DNA -> bacteriophages infect bacteria with geneCc material -> radioacCvity enters cell  ●Conclusion: geneCc material of bacteriophage was DNA not protein, DNA was the geneCc material found in genes, not just in viruses and bacteria, but in all living cells -> conﬁrmed Oswald Avery’s results  12.2 Structure of DNA Components of DNA  ●5C sugar (deoxyribose)  ●Phosphate Group","Viruses,infect,bacteria,Consists,protein,coat,DNA,RNA,core,ect,bacteria,bacteriophage,latch,onto,bacteria,bacteriophage,DNA,injected,cell,taking,bacteria,funcCons,host,bacteria,begin,producing,new,virus,parts,viruses,assembled,lling,bacteria,bacteria,explode,releases,new,viruses,Used,radioacCve,markers,isotopes,experiment,Sulfur,mark,protein,P,Phosphorus,mark,DNA,protein,coat,virus,bacteriophages,infect,bacteria,geneCc,material,radioacCvity,enters,P,mark,DNA,bacteriophages,infect,bacteria,geneCc,material,radioacCvity,enters,cell,Conclusion,geneCc,material,bacteriophage,DNA,protein,DNA,geneCc,material,found,genes,viruses,bacteria,living,cells,con,rmed,Oswald,Avery,results,Structure,DNA,Components,DNA,C,sugar,deoxyribose,Phosphate,Group"
