Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"13.2 Ribosomes and Protein Synthesis TranslaCon ●Make polypepCde chain using geneCc code on mRNA  ●By ribosome in cytoplasm  Proteins  ●4 levels of organizaCon 1.Sequence of amino acid in chain  2.Folding/Coiling of chain  3.Complete 3D arrangement (ionic, covalent, van der Waal forces, hydrogen bond)  4.More than one chain  PolypepCde ●Long chain of amino acids  ●Contain combinaCon of only 20 amino acids  ●Sequences of amino acid in polypepCde determine properCes, shape, funcCon of protein  GeneCc Code ●Codon: 3 consecuCve nucleoCde bases on mRNA (triplet), codes for single amino acid  ■Start Codon: AUG – methionine  ■Stop Codon: UAA/UAG/UGA  ●Some amino acids are universal -> can be coded by more than one codon","Ribosomes,Protein,Synthesis,TranslaCon,Make,polypepCde,chain,using,geneCc,code,mRNA,ribosome,cytoplasm,Proteins,levels,organizaCon,Sequence,amino,acid,chain,Folding,Coiling,chain,Complete,arrangement,ionic,covalent,van,der,Waal,forces,hydrogen,bond,one,chain,PolypepCde,Long,chain,amino,acids,Contain,combinaCon,amino,acids,Sequences,amino,acid,polypepCde,determine,properCes,shape,funcCon,protein,GeneCc,Code,Codon,consecuCve,nucleoCde,bases,mRNA,triplet,codes,single,amino,acid,Start,Codon,AUG,methionine,Stop,Codon,UAA,UAG,UGA,amino,acids,universal,coded,one,codon"
