Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Molecular Basis of Heredity ●The central dogma of molecular biology  ■GeneCc informaCon is transferred from DNA to RNA to protein  ●Genes contain instrucCon for making proteins  ■Enzymes catalyze ands regulate chemical reacCons  ■Build and operate on living cells  13.3 Muta)ons MutaCons: heritable changes in geneCc informaCon  ●Mutagens: chemical or physical agents in the environment that cause mutaCons  ●PesCcides, tobacco smoke, pollutants, X-rays, UV light  Types of MutaCons 1.Gene MutaCon: changes in one gene  2.Chromosomal MutaCon: changes in whole chromosome  Gene MutaCon  ●Point MutaCon: changes in one nucleoCde  1.Single base subsCtuCon: one nucleoCde base in replaced with another  2.Single base inserCon: one nucleoCde base added  3.Single base deleCon: one nucleoCde is removed","Molecular,Basis,Heredity,central,dogma,molecular,biology,GeneCc,informaCon,transferred,DNA,RNA,protein,Genes,contain,instrucCon,making,proteins,Enzymes,catalyze,ands,regulate,chemical,reacCons,Build,operate,living,cells,Muta,ons,MutaCons,heritable,changes,geneCc,informaCon,Mutagens,chemical,physical,agents,environment,cause,mutaCons,PesCcides,tobacco,smoke,pollutants,X,rays,UV,light,Types,MutaCons,Gene,MutaCon,changes,one,gene,Chromosomal,MutaCon,changes,whole,chromosome,Gene,MutaCon,Point,MutaCon,changes,one,nucleoCde,Single,base,subsCtuCon,one,nucleoCde,base,replaced,another,Single,base,inserCon,one,nucleoCde,base,added,Single,base,deleCon,one,nucleoCde,removed"
