Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"■  ■Polyploidy: have three or more sets of each type of chromosome (Triploid 3n, Tetraploid 4n) ◆Chromosome fail to separate in meiosis   ◆Polyploidy plants usually larger and stronger diploid plants  Eﬀects of MutaCons ●Many mutaCons are neutral -> have liile or no eﬀect on gene expression (protein funcCon)  ●Beneﬁcial MutaCons  ■Produce proteins with new acCviCes useful to organisms  ■Example: insects resist pesCcides, bacteria resist anCbioCcs  ■Source of geneCc variaCon (for evoluCon)  ●Harmful MutaCons  ■Progeria – causes children to age quickly  ■Sickle Cell Disease – point mutaCon  ■Marfan Syndrome  ■Albinism  ■Red-Green Colorblindness  ■Amyotrophic lateral Sclerosis (ALS) – causes the nerves that control muscle to stop working  13.4 Gene Regula)on and Expression ProkaryoCc Gene RegulaCon  ●DNA binding proteins in prokaryote -> regulate genes by controlling transcripCon  ●OrganizaCon of genes onto operons","Polyploidy,three,sets,type,chromosome,Triploid,n,Tetraploid,n,Chromosome,fail,separate,meiosis,Polyploidy,plants,usually,larger,stronger,diploid,plants,E,ects,MutaCons,Many,mutaCons,neutral,liile,e,ect,gene,expression,protein,funcCon,Bene,cial,MutaCons,Produce,proteins,new,acCviCes,useful,organisms,Example,insects,resist,pesCcides,bacteria,resist,anCbioCcs,Source,geneCc,variaCon,evoluCon,Harmful,MutaCons,Progeria,causes,children,age,quickly,Sickle,Cell,Disease,point,mutaCon,Marfan,Syndrome,Albinism,Red,Green,Colorblindness,Amyotrophic,lateral,Sclerosis,ALS,causes,nerves,control,muscle,stop,working,Gene,Regula,Expression,ProkaryoCc,Gene,RegulaCon,DNA,binding,proteins,prokaryote,regulate,genes,controlling,transcripCon,OrganizaCon,genes,onto,operons"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"■Operons: groups of genes that are regulated together  ■Example: the lac operon in E. coli  ◆Contain 3 lactose genes  ◆The three genes need to be expressed together (to produce proteins) so then the bacteria can digest lactose as food  ●Operon Structure: ■Promoter: RNA polymerase binding site. ■Operator: Repressor protein binding site. ■Genes: Cluster of functionally related genes (e.g., lactose metabolism genes in E. coli). 1.Eukaryotic Gene Regulation 2.RNA Interference (RNAi) Mechanism: Small interfering RNAs (siRNAs/miRNAs) form hairpin loops → diced by Dicer enzyme into 20-bp fragments. 3.Fragments load into a silencing complex → bind complementary mRNA → block translation/degrade mRNA. 4.Discovery (Fire & Mello, 1998): 5.Double-stranded RNA (dsRNA) injections caused gene silencing (unc-22gene in C. elegans → twitching). 6.Single-stranded RNA had no effect. 7.Significance: 8.Universal regulatory tool across life forms. 9.Medical potential: Silencing viral/cancer genes (RNAi technology). 10.Cell Specialization & Differentiation 11.Differentiation: Cells become specialized (e.g., liver vs. nerve cells) via selective gene expression. 12.Challenge: All cells share identical DNA; regulation enables diversity Genetic Control of Development Homeotic Genes •Function: Master switches determining body part identity (e.g., fruit fly leg vs. antenna). •Mutation Impact: Body part misplacement (e.g., leg growing from head).","Operons,groups,genes,regulated,together,Example,lac,operon,E,coli,Contain,lactose,genes,three,genes,need,expressed,together,produce,proteins,bacteria,digest,lactose,food,Operon,Structure,Promoter,RNA,polymerase,binding,site,Operator,Repressor,protein,binding,site,Genes,Cluster,functionally,related,genes,e,g,lactose,metabolism,genes,E,coli,Eukaryotic,Gene,Regulation,RNA,Interference,RNAi,Mechanism,Small,interfering,RNAs,siRNAs,miRNAs,form,hairpin,loops,diced,Dicer,enzyme,bp,fragments,Fragments,load,silencing,complex,bind,complementary,mRNA,block,translation,degrade,mRNA,Discovery,Fire,Mello,Double,stranded,RNA,dsRNA,injections,caused,gene,silencing,unc,gene,C,elegans,twitching,Single,stranded,RNA,effect,Significance,Universal,regulatory,tool,across,life,forms,Medical,potential,Silencing,viral,cancer,genes,RNAi,technology,Cell,Specialization,Differentiation,Differentiation,Cells,become,specialized,e,g,liver,vs,nerve,cells,via,selective,gene,expression,Challenge,cells,share,identical,DNA,regulation,enables,diversity,Genetic,Control,Development,Homeotic,Genes,Function,Master,switches,determining,body,part,identity,e,g,fruit,fly,leg,vs,antenna,Mutation,Impact,Body,part,misplacement,e,g,leg,growing,head"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Homeobox & Hox Genes •Homeobox: 180-bp DNA sequence coding for transcription factors that activate developmental genes. •Hox Genes: oSubgroup of homeobox genes; arranged in clusters (order correlates with body axis: head → tail). 13.Evolutionary Conservation: Identical clusters in fruit flies, mice, humans (e.g., control limb/fin development). 14.Role: Define segment identity (e.g., Hox mutations alter organ position).","Homeobox,Hox,Genes,Homeobox,bp,DNA,sequence,coding,transcription,factors,activate,developmental,genes,Hox,Genes,oSubgroup,homeobox,genes,arranged,clusters,order,correlates,body,axis,head,tail,Evolutionary,Conservation,Identical,clusters,fruit,flies,mice,humans,e,g,control,limb,fin,development,Role,Define,segment,identity,e,g,Hox,mutations,alter,organ,position"
