Review Practice.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"I. MCQ (60’, 1Q = 3’)   1. In Griffith’s experiment, all of the following would not cause mice to die EXCEPT: A) heat-killed S strain B) heat-killed S strain and living R strain C) living R strain D) heat-killed R strain  2. Avery proved DNA is genetic material because transformation failed in the test tube with: A) Proteinase B) ribonuclease C) deoxyribonuclease D) ligase  3. If Hershey-Chase found only S-35 radioactivity in bacteria, it would mean: A) Protein entered bacteria B) DNA contains genetic material C) Viruses lack DNA D) RNA carried genetic information  4. Chargaff's rules show that in DNA: A) A + G = T + C B) A = T and G = C C) Purines > Pyrimidines D) Bases absorb visible light  5. Rosalind Franklin's X-ray diffraction revealed DNA's: A) Nucleotide sequence B) Double-helix with bases near center C) Telomere function D) Transcription process  6. Topoisomerase prevents issues during replication by: A) Separating the double-helix structure B) Relieving overwinding strain C) Synthesizing primers D) Joining fragments  7. Telomerase inactivity in somatic cells causes: A) Limited cell division  B) Faster aging C) More mutations","MCQ,Q,Griffith,experiment,following,would,cause,mice,die,EXCEPT,heat,killed,strain,B,heat,killed,strain,living,R,strain,C,living,R,strain,heat,killed,R,strain,Avery,proved,DNA,genetic,material,transformation,failed,test,tube,Proteinase,B,ribonuclease,C,deoxyribonuclease,ligase,Hershey,Chase,found,radioactivity,bacteria,would,mean,Protein,entered,bacteria,B,DNA,contains,genetic,material,C,Viruses,lack,DNA,RNA,carried,genetic,information,Chargaff,rules,show,DNA,G,C,B,G,C,C,Purines,Pyrimidines,Bases,absorb,visible,light,Rosalind,Franklin,X,ray,diffraction,revealed,DNA,Nucleotide,sequence,B,Double,helix,bases,near,center,C,Telomere,function,Transcription,process,Topoisomerase,prevents,issues,replication,Separating,double,helix,structure,B,Relieving,overwinding,strain,C,Synthesizing,primers,Joining