H Reivew Practice.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"6. What is the molarity of a solu2on containing 0.5 moles of NaCl in 250 mL of water? A) 0.5 M B) 1.0 M C) 2.0 M D) 0.25 M 7. The First Law of Thermodynamics states that: A) Energy is conserved in an isolated system. B) Entropy always increases in a spontaneous process. C) Heat ﬂows from cold to hot objects. D) The enthalpy of a reac2on is path-independent. 8. The standard enthalpy of forma2on (ΔH°f) of an element in its most stable form is: A) Always posi2ve. B) Always nega2ve. C) Zero. D) Depends on temperature. 9. Which of the following is least soluble in water? A) CH3OH (methanol) B) C6H6 (benzene) C) NaCl D) NH3 10. Henry's Law states that the solubility of a gas in a liquid is directly propor2onal to: A) The temperature of the liquid. B) The par2al pressure of the gas above the liquid. C) The volume of the liquid. D) The density of the gas. 11. Why does NaCl dissolve well in water, but CCl4 does not? A) NaCl is nonpolar, while CCl4 is polar. B) NaCl dissociates into ions that interact with water’s dipole. C) CCl4 forms hydrogen bonds with water. D) Water has a lower dielectric constant than CCl4.","molarity,solu,containing,moles,NaCl,mL,water,B,C,First,Law,Thermodynamics,states,Energy,conserved,isolated,system,B,Entropy,always,increases,spontaneous,process,C,Heat,ows,cold,hot,objects,enthalpy,reac,path,independent,standard,enthalpy,forma,H,f,element,stable,form,Always,posi,B,Always,nega,C,Zero,Depends,temperature,following,least,soluble,water,CH,OH,methanol,B,C,H,benzene,C,NaCl,NH,Henry,Law,states,solubility,gas,liquid,directly,propor,onal,temperature,liquid,B,par,al,pressure,gas,liquid,C,volume,liquid,density,gas,NaCl,dissolve,well,water,CCl,NaCl,nonpolar,CCl,polar,B,NaCl,dissociates,ions,interact,water,dipole,C,CCl,forms,hydrogen,bonds,water,Water,lower,dielectric,constant,CCl"
