S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Chapter 15 Water and Aqueous Systems 15.1 Water and Its ProperBes  1. Bond polarity  • A nonpolar bond is a covalent bond formed when the atoms in the bond pull equally and the bonding electrons are shared equally.   • A polar bond is a covalent bond between atoms in which the electrons are shared unequally.   2. Polarity of molecules ➢ Most molecules with only nonpolar bonds are nonpolar. eg: H2 , C3H8  ➢ For molecules with polar bonds:  ✓Bent and pyramidal shape molecules must be polar.  ✓ When the “outside” atoms are idenBcal, molecules with linear, trigonal planar, tetrahedral shape are nonpolar.  1.Intermolecular forces  Three types: dispersion forces, dipole-dipole forces and hydrogen bonds.  (1)Dispersion Forces  (a) A symmetrical, spherical atom has no separaBon of charge.  (b) An atom can lose its spherical shape and become a temporary dipole, which has a","Chapter,Water,Aqueous,Systems,Water,ProperBes,Bond,polarity,nonpolar,bond,covalent,bond,formed,atoms,bond,pull,equally,bonding,electrons,shared,equally,polar,bond,covalent,bond,atoms,electrons,shared,unequally,Polarity,molecules,molecules,nonpolar,bonds,nonpolar,eg,H,C,H,molecules,polar,bonds,Bent,pyramidal,shape,molecules,must,polar,outside,atoms,idenBcal,molecules,linear,trigonal,planar,tetrahedral,shape,nonpolar,Intermolecular,forces,Three,types,dispersion,forces,dipole,dipole,forces,hydrogen,bonds,Dispersion,Forces,symmetrical,spherical,atom,separaBon,charge,b,atom,lose,spherical,shape,become,temporary,dipole"
S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"separaBon of opposite charge.  (c) A temporary dipole creates an induced dipole in the adjacent atoms.   Induced Dipole: a dipole that is created by the presence of a neighboring dipole. Dispersion Force: a force of a`racBon between induced dipoles.  -The boiling point of a liquid is a measure of the strength of the a`racBve forces between molecules in the liquid state. The stronger the a`racBve forces, the higher boiling point. -As the size of atoms increase, boiling point increases. -Dispersion forces increase with increasing molecular/atomic size and mass (2)Dipole-dipole forces  a.Polar molecules have permanent dipoles.  b.dipole-dipole forces: a`racBon between opposite charges of neighboring permanent dipoles. (3)Hydrogen Bonding  -In a covalent bond H—X (X is N, O or F), the parBal charges (δ+ andδ- ) are parBcular large due to the large diﬀerence in electronegaBviBes between H and X. 4. Water molecules  -high surface tension, low vapor pressure, and high boiling point—result from hydrogen bonding 5. Surface Tension -The inward force, or pull, that tends to minimize the surface area of a liquid is called surface tension. • A surfactant is any substance that interferes with the hydrogen bonding between water molecules and thereby reduces surface tension.  • Soaps and detergents are surfactants","separaBon,opposite,charge,c,temporary,dipole,creates,induced,dipole,adjacent,atoms,Induced,Dipole,dipole,created,presence,neighboring,dipole,Dispersion,Force,force,racBon,induced,dipoles,boiling,point,liquid,measure,strength,racBve,forces,molecules,liquid,state,stronger,racBve,forces,higher,boiling,point,size,atoms,increase,boiling,point,increases,Dispersion,forces,increase,increasing,molecular,atomic,size,mass,Dipole,dipole,forces,Polar,molecules,permanent,dipoles,b,dipole,dipole,forces,racBon,opposite,charges,neighboring,permanent,dipoles,Hydrogen,Bonding,covalent,bond,H,X,X,N,F,parBal,charges,parBcular,large,due,large,di,erence,electronegaBviBes,H,X,Water,molecules,high,surface,tension,low,vapor,pressure,high,boiling,point,result,hydrogen,bonding,Surface,Tension,inward,force,pull,tends,minimize,surface,area,liquid,called,surface,tension,surfactant,substance,interferes,hydrogen,bonding,water,molecules,thereby,reduces,surface,tension,Soaps,detergents,surfactants"
S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"6.Vapor Pressure  Hydrogen bonding between water molecules also explains water’s unusually low vapor pressure.  • An extensive network of hydrogen bonds holds the molecules in liquid water to one another.  • These hydrogen bonds must be broken before water changes from the liquid to the vapor state, so the tendency of these molecules to escape is low and evaporaBon is slow.  7. Density  -ice less dense than liquid water. -Ice has a hexagonal structure. Extensive hydrogen bonding in ice holds the water molecules farther apart in a more ordered arrangement than in liquid water. 15.2 Homogeneous Aqueous Systems  I. SoluBons  • aqueous soluBon: a soluBon with water as the solvent.   -Solute is normally:  1)the component whose original state is diﬀerent from the state of soluBon  2) or the one that present in small amount.","Vapor,Pressure,Hydrogen,bonding,water,molecules,also,explains,water,unusually,low,vapor,pressure,extensive,network,hydrogen,bonds,holds,molecules,liquid,water,one,another,hydrogen,bonds,must,broken,water,changes,liquid,vapor,state,tendency,molecules,escape,low,evaporaBon,slow,Density,ice,less,dense,liquid,water,Ice,hexagonal,structure,Extensive,hydrogen,bonding,ice,holds,water,molecules,farther,apart,ordered,arrangement,liquid,water,Homogeneous,Aqueous,Systems,SoluBons,aqueous,soluBon,soluBon,water,solvent,Solute,normally,component,whose,original,state,di,erent,state,soluBon,one,present,small,amount"
S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"SolvaCon : the process of surrounding solute parBcles with solvent parBcles to form a soluBon.  Electrolytes and Nonelectrolytes  electrolyte: a compound that conducts an electric current when it is in an aqueous soluBon or in the molten state.  e.g., all ionic compounds, some molecular compounds(most acids or bases, water), etc.  nonelectrolyte: a compound that does not conduct an electric current in either an aqueous soluBon or the molten state.  – Some polar molecular compounds are nonelectrolytes in the pure state but become electrolytes when they dissolve in water.  E.g., ammonia (NH3 (g)) is not an electrolyte in the pure state.   Hydrates  Hydrate: a compound that contains H2O units within its crystal structure.   -the water is easily lost and regained.","SolvaCon,process,surrounding,solute,parBcles,solvent,parBcles,form,soluBon,Electrolytes,Nonelectrolytes,electrolyte,compound,conducts,electric,current,aqueous,soluBon,molten,state,e,g,ionic,compounds,molecular,compounds,acids,bases,water,etc,nonelectrolyte,compound,conduct,electric,current,either,aqueous,soluBon,molten,state,polar,molecular,compounds,nonelectrolytes,pure,state,become,electrolytes,dissolve,water,E,g,ammonia,NH,g,electrolyte,pure,state,Hydrates,Hydrate,compound,contains,H,units,within,crystal,structure,water,easily,lost,regained"
