S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"3. Emulsions DeﬁniCon: A colloidal dispersion of a liquid in a liquid. Emulsifying Agent: EssenBal for formaBon and stability of emulsions.  Example: Soap or detergent. Soap molecules have a polar end (a`racted to water) and a nonpolar end (a`racted to oil or grease). Examples of Emulsions:Oil and water with soap, Mayonnaise. 4. ProperBes of SoluBons, Colloids, and Suspensions System TypeDispersed PhaseDispersion MediumExamplesGas in LiquidGasLiquidWhipped creamGas in SolidGasSolidMarshmallowLiquid in LiquidLiquidLiquidMilk, mayonnaiseLiquid in GasLiquidGasFog, aerosolSolid in GasSolidGasSmoke, dust in airSolid in LiquidSolidLiquidPaint, blood, starch in water","Emulsions,De,niCon,colloidal,dispersion,liquid,liquid,Emulsifying,Agent,EssenBal,formaBon,stability,emulsions,Example,Soap,detergent,Soap,molecules,polar,end,racted,water,nonpolar,end,racted,oil,grease,Examples,Emulsions,Oil,water,soap,Mayonnaise,ProperBes,SoluBons,Colloids,Suspensions,System,TypeDispersed,PhaseDispersion,MediumExamplesGas,LiquidGasLiquidWhipped,creamGas,SolidGasSolidMarshmallowLiquid,LiquidLiquidLiquidMilk,mayonnaiseLiquid,GasLiquidGasFog,aerosolSolid,GasSolidGasSmoke,dust,airSolid,LiquidSolidLiquidPaint,blood,starch,water"
