S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"water and ethanol). Immiscible Liquids: Liquids that do not dissolve in each other (e.g., oil and water). 3. Factors AﬀecBng Solubility (1) Temperature The solubility of solid, liquid, and gaseous solutes is aﬀected by temperature:  Solids: Solubility generally increases with temperature. Gases: Solubility decreases with increasing temperature (e.g., carbonated beverages go ﬂat more quickly at room temperature). (2) Pressure (Henry’s Law)","water,ethanol,Immiscible,Liquids,Liquids,dissolve,e,g,oil,water,Factors,ecBng,Solubility,Temperature,solubility,solid,liquid,gaseous,solutes,ected,temperature,Solids,Solubility,generally,increases,temperature,Gases,Solubility,decreases,increasing,temperature,e,g,carbonated,beverages,go,quickly,room,temperature,Pressure,Henry,Law"
