S Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"also known as molal concentraBon. Mole FracCon (X) of a solute in a soluBon is the raBo of moles of the solute to the total number of moles of solvent and solute.   Where:  XA = mole fracBon of solute A, XB = mole fracBon of solvent B nA = moles of solute, nB = moles of solvent 2. Freezing-Point Depression and Boiling-Point ElevaBon Freezing-Point Depression (ΔTf) Freezing-point depression is the diﬀerence between the freezing point of the soluBon and the freezing point of the pure solvent. Formula: ΔTf = Kf × m  Kf = molal freezing-point depression constant m = molality Boiling-Point ElevaCon (ΔTb) Boiling-point elevaBon is the diﬀerence between the boiling point of the soluBon and the boiling point of the pure solvent. Formula: ΔTb = Kb × m  Kb = molal boiling-point elevaBon constant m = molality Constants (Kf and Kb)","also,known,molal,concentraBon,Mole,FracCon,X,solute,soluBon,raBo,moles,solute,total,number,moles,solvent,solute,XA,mole,fracBon,solute,XB,mole,fracBon,solvent,B,nA,moles,solute,nB,moles,solvent,Freezing,Point,Depression,Boiling,Point,ElevaBon,Freezing,Point,Depression,Tf,Freezing,point,depression,di,erence,freezing,point,soluBon,freezing,point,pure,solvent,Formula,Tf,Kf,Kf,molal,freezing,point,depression,constant,molality,Boiling,Point,ElevaCon,Tb,Boiling,point,elevaBon,di,erence,boiling,point,soluBon,boiling,point,pure,solvent,Formula,Tb,Kb,Kb,molal,boiling,point,elevaBon,constant,molality,Constants,Kf,Kb"
