H Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Database ●Organized, shared collection of data for long term use  ●Database Management System (DBMS) is software used to manage databases for data definition, data manipulation, data control ●Database System (DBS) encompasses data, DBMS, application programs using the data and users interacting with it Relational Database: most prevalent type of databases ●Store data in tables, and relationships between tables are established through common fields ●SQL (Structure Query Language) Basic Definition Language 1.INSERT INTO: Inserts new rows INSERT INTO Student (SID, Stu_Name, Gender, DOB, Nationality)  V ALUES (1009, 'John', 'M', '2004-07-15', 'UK') Ex: INSERT INTO GFG_Employees (id, name, email, department)  V ALUES  (1, 'Jessie', 'jessie23@gmail.com', 'Development'),","Database,Organized,shared,collection,data,long,term,use,Database,Management,System,DBMS,software,used,manage,databases,data,definition,data,manipulation,data,control,Database,System,DBS,encompasses,data,DBMS,application,programs,using,data,users,interacting,Relational,Database,prevalent,type,databases,Store,data,tables,relationships,tables,established,common,fields,SQL,Structure,Query,Language,Basic,Definition,Language,INSERT,Inserts,new,rows,INSERT,Student,SID,Stu,Name,Gender,DOB,Nationality,V,ALUES,John,UK,Ex,INSERT,GFG,Employees,id,name,email,department,V,ALUES,Jessie,jessie,gmail,com,Development"
