AP Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"2. Monopsony MFC= Marginal Factor Cost MRP: Marginal revenue product In perfectly compeEEon, the labor market set a price, and this price is the MFC for individual ﬁrms. The Demand for Labor in individual ﬁrms, which is the MRP of it, is sloping downward. The ﬁrm are price taker and they will hire at the quanEty where the MRP meet the MFC. In Monopsony, the ﬁrm is the only ﬁrm in a labor market. This cause it to control the wage. It produces at the quanEty where MFC=Demand (MRP), and the price is the intersecEon point between Supply curve and the quanEty produced.","Monopsony,MFC,Marginal,Factor,Cost,MRP,Marginal,revenue,product,perfectly,compeEEon,labor,market,set,price,price,MFC,individual,rms,Demand,Labor,individual,rms,MRP,sloping,downward,rm,price,taker,hire,quanEty,MRP,meet,MFC,Monopsony,rm,rm,labor,market,cause,control,wage,produces,quanEty,MFC,Demand,MRP,price,intersecEon,point,Supply,curve,quanEty,produced"
