H Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"barren that it looked like the moon.  Constrict - To tighten, squeeze, or flatten - He walked  closer, and I felt the world constrict, my heart pulsing against my  ribs. When we were only an arm’s length apart, he stopped. Excruciating - Extremely intense or  painful - It was a lovely thought, but  hearing Arturo’s optimism bubble to the  surface, hearing the rawness of it, was  excruciating.  Console -to comfort - At the hospital, Officer Mora, the same officer I  had spoken with at the station months earlier, tried to console me.  Indisputable - not able to dispute or  argue against. - “She’s getting better,”  I said, as if by repeating it enough, I  could somehow make it part of the  public record, an indisputable fact. (Quizlet for vocab for practice): Click here If it doesn’t work then use this link: https://quizlet.com/cn/1052411741/final-h-level-vocab-flash-cards/?i=3eosgh&x=1qqt","barren,looked,like,moon,Constrict,tighten,squeeze,flatten,walked,closer,felt,world,constrict,heart,pulsing,ribs,arm,length,apart,stopped,Excruciating,Extremely,intense,painful,lovely,thought,hearing,Arturo,optimism,bubble,surface,hearing,rawness,excruciating,Console,comfort,hospital,Officer,Mora,officer,spoken,station,months,earlier,tried,console,Indisputable,able,dispute,argue,getting,better,said,repeating,enough,could,somehow,make,part,public,record,indisputable,fact,Quizlet,vocab,practice,Click,work,use,link,https,quizlet,com,cn,final,h,level,vocab,flash,cards,eosgh,x,qqt"
