H+ Practice Set .pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"1.  What ini/ally prompts Daniel Quinn to take on the role of a detec/ve?     a) A newspaper adver/sement     b) A leYer from Peter S/llman Jr.     c) A misdirected phone call for ""Paul Auster, Private Inves/gator""     d) A request from the real Paul Auster 2.  Peter S/llman Sr.'s horriﬁc experiments on his son were primarily focused on:     a) Physical strength and endurance     b) Developing psychic abili/es     c) Proving a theory about language and the pre-Babel state     d) Crea/ng a perfect heir to his fortune 3.  What recurring visual mo/f is used to symbolize Quinn's psychological breakdown and the labyrinthine nature of reality?     a) Floa/ng eyeballs     b) ShaYered glass     c) Mazes, spirals, and fragmented panels     d) Flowing water      4.  How does the graphic novel primarily end for Daniel Quinn?     a) He solves the case and returns to wri/ng.     b) He confronts and defeats S/llman Sr.","ini,ally,prompts,Daniel,Quinn,take,role,detec,newspaper,adver,sement,b,leYer,Peter,llman,Jr,c,misdirected,phone,call,Paul,Auster,Private,Inves,gator,request,real,Paul,Auster,Peter,llman,Sr,horri,c,experiments,son,primarily,focused,Physical,strength,endurance,b,Developing,psychic,abili,es,c,Proving,theory,language,pre,Babel,state,Crea,ng,perfect,heir,fortune,recurring,visual,mo,f,used,symbolize,Quinn,psychological,breakdown,labyrinthine,nature,reality,Floa,ng,eyeballs,b,ShaYered,glass,c,Mazes,spirals,fragmented,panels,Flowing,water,graphic,novel,primarily,end,Daniel,Quinn,solves,case,returns,wri,ng,b,confronts,defeats,llman,Sr"
