H+ Practice Set .pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"8.  What does Quinn's red notebook symbolize throughout the story?     a) His ﬁnancial success as a writer     b) His connec/on to his deceased son     c) His desperate aYempt to impose order, meaning, and iden/ty through language – which ul/mately fails     d) The clues leading to S/llman Sr.'s capture 9.  The graphic novel fundamentally subverts the tradi/onal detec/ve genre by:     a) Having the detec/ve solve mul/ple complex cases     b) Making the detec/ve a ﬂamboyant superhero     c) Depic/ng the detec/ve's uYer failure, mental disintegra/on, and the unsolvable nature of the mystery     d) Senng the story in a fantas/cal world instead of a city 10. The visual depic/on of New York City in the graphic novel primarily emphasizes:     a) Its vibrant nightlife and tourist aYrac/ons     b) Its role as a warm, suppor/ve community     c) Its vastness, anonymity, labyrinthine quali/es, and func/on as a character inducing aliena/on     d) Its futuris/c technology and architecture Free Response Ques/ons (FRQs)","Quinn,red,notebook,symbolize,throughout,story,nancial,success,writer,b,connec,deceased,son,c,desperate,aYempt,impose,order,meaning,iden,ty,language,ul,mately,fails,clues,leading,llman,Sr,capture,graphic,novel,fundamentally,subverts,tradi,onal,detec,genre,detec,solve,mul,ple,complex,cases,b,Making,detec,amboyant,superhero,c,Depic,ng,detec,uYer,failure,mental,disintegra,unsolvable,nature,mystery,Senng,story,fantas,cal,world,instead,city,visual,depic,New,York,City,graphic,novel,primarily,emphasizes,vibrant,nightlife,tourist,aYrac,ons,b,role,warm,suppor,community,c,vastness,anonymity,labyrinthine,quali,es,func,character,inducing,aliena,futuris,c,technology,architecture,Free,Response,Ques,ons,FRQs"
H+ Practice Set .pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"1.  Trace Daniel Quinn's psychological and physical descent throughout the graphic novel. What key events and realiza/ons contribute to his ul/mate breakdown and disappearance?         2.  Analyze how David Mazzucchelli's artwork contributes signiﬁcantly to the themes of City of Glass. Choose TWO speciﬁc themes (e.g., Iden/ty, Reality vs. Illusion, Language/Failure, Aliena/on) and explain how visual elements (panel layout, shading, symbolism, character design, pacing) enhance them.         3.  Discuss how City of Glass func/ons as a deconstruc/on or subversion of the tradi/onal detec/ve genre. What conven/onal tropes does it use, and how does it ul/mately undermine or reject them?         4.  Explore the theme of ""authorship"" within City of Glass. Consider the roles of Daniel Quinn, the real Paul Auster (character), Paul Auster (original author), and Paul Karasik & David Mazzucchelli (adapters). How does the graphic novel comment on the nature of crea/ng stories and iden//es?","Trace,Daniel,Quinn,psychological,physical,descent,throughout,graphic,novel,key,events,realiza,ons,contribute,ul,mate,breakdown,disappearance,Analyze,David,Mazzucchelli,artwork,contributes,signi,cantly,themes,City,Glass,Choose,TWO,speci,c,themes,e,g,Iden,ty,Reality,vs,Illusion,Language,Failure,Aliena,explain,visual,elements,panel,layout,shading,symbolism,character,design,pacing,enhance,Discuss,City,Glass,func,ons,deconstruc,subversion,tradi,onal,detec,genre,conven,onal,tropes,use,ul,mately,undermine,reject,Explore,theme,authorship,within,City,Glass,Consider,roles,Daniel,Quinn,real,Paul,Auster,character,Paul,Auster,original,author,Paul,Karasik,David,Mazzucchelli,adapters,graphic,novel,comment,nature,crea,ng,stories,iden,es"
