H+ Practice Set Answers.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"•Paul Auster (Original Author): Created the source novel. His presence as a character blurs lines between creator and crea/on. The story explores themes he wrote about. •Karasik & Mazzucchelli (Adapters): ""Authors"" of the graphic novel version. Their choices (visual style, condensa/on, emphasis) reinterpret Auster's work, demonstra/ng adapta/on as a form of authorship/crea/on. •Commentary: The graphic novel suggests iden//es are constructed like stories (Quinn's personas). Authorship is unstable (pseudonyms, adapta/ons). Trying to control a narra/ve (life or story) can lead to failure and dissolu/on. Crea/on involves layers of iden/ty and interpreta/on.","Paul,Auster,Original,Author,Created,source,novel,presence,character,blurs,lines,creator,crea,story,explores,themes,wrote,Karasik,Mazzucchelli,Adapters,Authors,graphic,novel,version,choices,visual,style,condensa,emphasis,reinterpret,Auster,work,demonstra,ng,adapta,form,authorship,crea,Commentary,graphic,novel,suggests,iden,es,constructed,like,stories,Quinn,personas,Authorship,unstable,pseudonyms,adapta,ons,Trying,control,narra,life,story,lead,failure,dissolu,Crea,involves,layers,iden,ty,interpreta"
