H+ Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Lexis Terms: •Border – The line or frame around a comic panel. •GuWer – The space between comic panels where the reader infers movement or Dme passing. •Speech Bubble – A rounded shape that contains a character's spoken words. •Emanata – Visual symbols (e.g., sweat drops, moDon lines) showing emoDon or movement. •Tier – A horizontal row of comic panels. •Icon – A simpliﬁed image that represents a character, object, or idea. •Sound Eﬀect – Onomatopoeic words (e.g., BOOM, splash) that convey sound within the scene. •CapDon – Text (o`en in a box) that provides narraDon or context outside of dialogue. •Postmodernism: A literary movement marked by skepDcism, irony, and rejecDon of universal truths or grand narraDves. •FragmentaDon: A narraDve technique breaking structure, Dme, or character conDnuity into disjointed parts. •Meaning: O`en quesDoned or destabilized in postmodern texts, suggesDng mulDple or no ﬁxed interpretaDons. •Irony: The use of language or structure to express something opposite or contradictory to the expected meaning. •Intertextuality: Referencing or integraDng other texts within a text to create new layers of meaning. •Genre: A category or type of literature; postmodernism o`en blends or disrupts genres. •Subversion: Undermining tradiDonal norms, values, or expectaDons, o`en with a criDcal or saDrical edge. •Text/Paratext: The main body of a work (text) and supplementary materials like Dtles, forewords, or footnotes (paratext) that shape interpretaDon.  Core Informa1on: •Original Author: Paul Auster (from The New York Trilogy) •Adaptors: Paul Karasik (Writer/Adapter), David Mazzucchelli (ArDst) •Genre: Postmodern Mystery / ExistenDal Graphic Novel / Literary AdaptaDon •Key Themes: IdenDty, Language, Reality vs. Illusion, Authorship, Obsession, Urban AlienaDon, Failure. Plot & Premise: •Daniel Quinn, a lonely mystery writer grieving his wife and son, receives a wrong-number call meant for ""Paul Auster, Private InvesDgator."" •Intrigued/desperate, Quinn becomes ""Paul Auster"" and takes the case from the disturbed Peter SDllman Jr. •The case: Protect Peter SDllman Jr. from his recently released father, Peter SDllman Sr., who subjected Peter Jr. to horriﬁc language-deprivaDon experiments. •Quinn begins obsessively trailing the enigmaDc and seemingly harmless SDllman Sr. through NYC.","Lexis,Terms,Border,line,frame,around,comic,panel,GuWer,space,comic,panels,reader,infers,movement,Dme,passing,Speech,Bubble,rounded,shape,contains,character,spoken,words,Emanata,Visual,symbols,e,g,sweat,drops,moDon,lines,showing,emoDon,movement,Tier,horizontal,row,comic,panels,Icon,simpli,ed,image,represents,character,object,idea,Sound,E,ect,Onomatopoeic,words,e,g,BOOM,splash,convey,sound,within,scene,CapDon,Text,en,box,provides,narraDon,context,outside,dialogue,Postmodernism,literary,movement,marked,skepDcism,irony,rejecDon,universal,truths,grand,narraDves,FragmentaDon,narraDve,technique,breaking,structure,Dme,character,conDnuity,disjointed,parts,Meaning,en,quesDoned,destabilized,postmodern,texts,suggesDng,mulDple,xed,interpretaDons,Irony,use,language,structure,express,something,opposite,contradictory,expected,meaning,Intertextuality,Referencing,integraDng,texts,within,text,create,new,layers,meaning,Genre,category,type,literature,postmodernism,en,blends,disrupts,genres,Subversion,Undermining,tradiDonal,norms,values,expectaDons,en,criDcal,saDrical,edge,Text,Paratext,main,body,work,text,supplementary,materials,like,Dtles,forewords,footnotes,paratext,shape,interpretaDon,Core,Informa,Original,Author,Paul,Auster,New,York,Trilogy,Adaptors,Paul,Karasik,Writer,Adapter,David,Mazzucchelli,ArDst,Genre,Postmodern,Mystery,ExistenDal,Graphic,Novel,Literary,AdaptaDon,Key,Themes,IdenDty,Language,Reality,vs,Illusion,Authorship,Obsession,Urban,AlienaDon,Failure,Plot,Premise,Daniel,Quinn,lonely,mystery,writer,grieving,wife,son,receives,wrong,number,call,meant,Paul,Auster,Private,InvesDgator,Intrigued,desperate,