AP Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"•Increased cultural diffusion9.2 Technological Advances and Limitations After 1900: DiseaseKey Concepts:•Medical advances increased survival, but some diseases spread more quickly due to globalization.Diseases:•New Epidemics: HIV/AIDS, Ebola, COVID-19•Lifestyle-Related Diseases: Diabetes, heart disease, Alzheimer’s•Poverty-Associated Diseases: Tuberculosis, malaria, choleraImpact:•International organizations (e.g., WHO) began coordinated global health responses.•Global inequalities in health persisted.9.3 Technological Advances: Debates About the Environment After 1900Environmental Issues:•Climate Change•Deforestation•Air/Water Pollution•Desertiﬁcation•Loss of BiodiversityResponses:•Green Revolution: Increased agricultural output using GMO seeds, pesticides, and irrigation.•Environmental Movements: Earth Day (1970), Greenpeace•International Agreements: Kyoto Protocol (1997), Paris Agreement (2015)Signiﬁcance:•Sparked debate over development vs. sustainability•Created tension between developed and developing nations9.4 Economic Globalization","Increased,cultural,diffusion,Technological,Advances,Limitations,DiseaseKey,Concepts,Medical,advances,increased,survival,diseases,spread,quickly,due,globalization,Diseases,New,Epidemics,HIV,AIDS,Ebola,COVID,Lifestyle,Related,Diseases,Diabetes,heart,disease,Alzheimer,Poverty,Associated,Diseases,Tuberculosis,malaria,choleraImpact,International,organizations,e,g,began,coordinated,global,health,responses,Global,inequalities,health,persisted,Technological,Advances,Debates,Environment,Environmental,Issues,Climate,Change,Deforestation,Air,Water,Pollution,Deserti,cation,Loss,BiodiversityResponses,Green,Revolution,Increased,agricultural,output,using,GMO,seeds,pesticides,irrigation,Environmental,Movements,Earth,Day,Greenpeace,International,Agreements,Kyoto,Protocol,Paris,Agreement,Signi,cance,Sparked,debate,development,vs,sustainability,Created,tension,developed,developing,nations,Economic,Globalization"
