AP Precalculus Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,- The tangent function and the inverse tangent function 8.2 Sine and cosine curves - Frequency: The frequency of a sinusoidal function is the number of cycles that its graph completes in an interval of 2𝜋 radians. - Amplitude: The amplitude of a sinusoidal function is half the difference between its maximum and minimum values. - Midline: The midline of the graph of a sinusoidal function is determined by the average of the maximum and minimum values of the function.,"tangent,function,inverse,tangent,function,Sine,cosine,curves,Frequency,frequency,sinusoidal,function,number,cycles,graph,completes,interval,radians,Amplitude,amplitude,sinusoidal,function,half,difference,maximum,minimum,values,Midline,midline,graph,sinusoidal,function,determined,average,maximum,minimum,values,function"
