Practice Set Answers.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Fill in the blanks with one of the following: impressionism, primitivism, expressionism, minimalism, electronic and chance music minimalism Categorized by repetition with gradual changes impressionism Often uses pentatonic, modal, and whole-tone scales. electronic and chance music When some elements of the composition are determined by chance primitivism Uses prehistoric themes and tribal rhythms.  expressionism Uses the 12-tone system (atonality) expressionism Often makes use of polytonality impressionism Key figure: Claude Debussy electronic music Uses tape loops and synthesizers minimalism An example of this would be Steve Reich’s Clapping Music expressionism Music from this category is often anxiety-inducing and spooky   Fill in the blanks with one of the following: string, woodwind, brass, percussion, keyboard, and electronic 1.Trumpet brass 2.Harpsichord keyboard 3.Flute woodwind 4.organ keyboard 5.Bassoon woodwind 6.Violin string Key features?Religious, sacred, Neumes: Early notation, church modes More secular but mostly sacred and modal, harmony development, Realistic, linear perspective in art, Word painting: Music illustrates lyrics (e.g., “ascending” = rising pitch).Terraced dynamic, basso continuo, unity of mood, rhythmic drive, dramatic artBalanced phrases, simple harmony, clear cadences.Love, death, nature, the supernatural, exoticism.","Fill,blanks,one,following,impressionism,primitivism,expressionism,minimalism,electronic,chance,music,minimalism,Categorized,repetition,gradual,changes,impressionism,Often,uses,pentatonic,modal,whole,tone,scales,electronic,chance,music,elements,composition,determined,chance,primitivism,Uses,prehistoric,themes,tribal,rhythms,expressionism,Uses,tone,system,atonality,expressionism,Often,makes,use,polytonality,impressionism,Key,figure,Claude,Debussy,electronic,music,Uses,tape,loops,synthesizers,minimalism,example,would,Steve,Reich,Clapping,Music,expressionism,Music,category,ofte