Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Unit 1: Line & TextureLINE A mark or Troke made (with pen, pencil, paint, etc.) to show movement, an objeM’s placement, or to communicate a visual feeling. ✓ Depending on the way line is used in a composiCon, the arCT has the ability to useline to communicate a speciﬁc emoCon: ◆ VerCcal Line: Stability/StruMure/Power ◆ Horizontal Line: ReT/RelaxaCon/Calmness ◆ Curving Line: Movement/Sporadic/Energy ◆ Diagonal Line: Unbalanced/ChaoCc ◆ Contour (Line): The outline; the edge or line that deﬁnes or bounds a shape or objeM. ✓ ObjeMs would not be visible to the human eye without a contour:² In a 2 dimensional drawing/painCng, the contour lines can be considered the objeM(s) outline.²  In a real (3 dimensional) objeM, the contour is simply the line that deﬁnes itsedges.² Implied Line: Line that doesn’t physically exiT but is implied to exiT TEXTURE A visual caraMerisCc of the relaConship between the way an objeM looks and feels (by touc). ✓ Visual texture is used in art to also communicate an idea or emoCon.  COMPOSITION A visual caraMerisCc of the relaConship between the way an objeM looks and feels.","Unit,Line,TextureLINE,mark,Troke,made,pen,pencil,paint,etc,show,movement,objeM,placement,communicate,visual,feeling,Depending,way,line,used,composiCon,arCT,ability,useline,communicate,speci,c,emoCon,VerCcal,Line,Stability,StruMure,Power,Horizontal,Line,ReT,RelaxaCon,Calmness,Curving,Line,Movement,Sporadic,Energy,Diagonal,Line,Unbalanced,ChaoCc,Contour,Line,outline,edge,line,de,nes,bounds,shape,objeM,ObjeMs,would,visible,human,eye,without,contour,dimensional,drawing,painCng,contour,lines,considered,objeM,outline,real,dimensional,objeM,contour,simply,line,de,nes,itsedges,Implied,Line,Line,physically,exiT,implied,exiT,TEXTURE,visual,caraMerisCc,relaConship,way,objeM,looks,feels,touc,Visual,texture,used,art,also,communicate,idea,emoCon,COMPOSITION,visual,caraMerisCc,relaConship,way,objeM,looks,feels"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"OVERLAP When an objeM(s) covers or parCally covers another objeM in a composiCon to convey the idea of space. ✓ Overlapping helps to communicate depth and a sense of real space in a composiCon. REPETITION When something is repeated or occurs over and over again in the same composiCon. ✓ Using repeCCon within a composiCon helps to give the composiCon unity and consiTency. ◆ Edgar Degas: A Frenc arCT famous for his painCngs, sculptures, prints, and drawings. ◆ Andy Warhol: An American arCT, direMor, and producer who was a leading ﬁgure in the visual art movement known as pop art. ◆ Henri Ma5sse: A Frenc arCT, known for his use of color and his ﬂuid and original draughtsmanship. A draughtsman, printmaker, and sculptor, but is known primarily as a painter. Unit 2: Color & Value COLOR (HUE) The amount of light reﬂeMed on an objeM. ✓ The only way the color of an objeM can be seen depends on the amount of light reﬂeMed on its surface 1. Primary Colors: Natural/basic colors that can’t be created with the combinaCon of other colors.","OVERLAP,objeM,covers,parCally,covers,another,objeM,composiCon,convey,idea,space,Overlapping,helps,communicate,depth,sense,real,space,composiCon,REPETITION,something,repeated,occurs,composiCon,Using,repeCCon,within,composiCon,helps,give,composiCon,unity,consiTency,Edgar,Degas,Frenc,arCT,famous,painCngs,sculptures,prints,drawings,Andy,Warhol,American,arCT,direMor,producer,leading,gure,visual,art,movement,known,pop,art,Henri,sse,Frenc,arCT,known,use,color,uid,original,draughtsmanship,draughtsman,printmaker,sculptor,known,primarily,painter,Unit,Color,Value,COLOR,HUE,amount,light,eMed,objeM,way,color,objeM,seen,depends,amount,light,eMed,surface,Primary,Colors,Natural,basic,colors,created,combinaCon,colors"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"2. Secondary Colors: The combinaCon of two primary colors. 3. TerCary Colors: The combinaCon of a primary color and a secondary color. VALUE (TINT, TONE, & SHADE) The degree of lightness or darkness within a given color, shade, tone or Cnt. ✓ Changing a color’s value usually makes the color seem less intense or subtle. ◆ Shade: Blaf; the value of a color becomes darker depending on the degree of shade used with that color. ◆ Tone: Grey; the value of a color becomes grayer depending on the degree of tone used with that color. ◆ Tint: White; the value of a color becomes lighter depending on the degree of Cnt used with that color. ◆ Mono0roma3c (单⾊模式)² The use of a wide range of Cnts and shades of a single color. Harmonious & Subtle ◆ Complementary (互补⾊模式)²  The use of opposite colors on the color wheel.  Very Vibrant ◆ Analogous (相似⾊模式)²  The use of a set of colors that are adjacent to eac other on the color wheel.²  Harmonious & Subtle ◆ Split Complementary (补⾊分割模式)²  The combinaCon of complementary and analogous scemes that allows intensity but is not as Trong as pure complementary.²  Vibrant & Harmonious","Secondary,Colors,The,combinaCon,of,two,primary,colors,TerCary,Colors,The,combinaCon,of,a,primary,color,and,a,secondary,color,VALUE,TINT,TONE,SHADE,The,degree,of,lightness,or,darkness,within,a,given,color,shade,tone,or,Cnt,Changing,a,color,s,value,usually,makes,the,color,seem,less,intense,or,subtle,Shade,Blaf,the,value,of,a,color,becomes,darker,depending,on,the,degree,of,shade,used,with,that,color,Tone,Grey,the,value,of,a,color,becomes,grayer,depending,on,the,degree,of,tone,used,with,that,color,Tint,White,the,value,of,a,color,becomes,lighter,depending,on,the,degree,of,Cnt,used,with,that,color,Mono,roma,c,单,模式,The,use,of,a,wide,range,of,Cnts,and,shades,of,a,single,color,Harmonious,Subtle,Complementary,互补,模式,The,use,of,opposite,colors,on,the,color,wheel,Very,Vibrant,Analogous,相似,模式,The,use,of,a,set,of,colors,that,are,adjacent,to