Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"◆ Triadic (三等分配⾊模式)²  The use of three colors equally spaced around the color wheel.² Vibrant & Harmonious BALANCE Arranging elements in a composiCon so that no one part of a work overpowers, or seem sheavier than any other part. ✓ Balance is a principle of design that deals with the visual weight within a composiCon. ◆ Symmetrical²  A balance that shows Tability, usually centered in the composiCon. ◆ VerCcal²  A type of symmetrical balance that shows a verCcal orientaCon. ◆ Horizontal²  A type of symmetrical balance that shows a horizontal orientaCon. ◆ Asymmetrical²  A balance that is not centered and not symmetrical. ◆ Radial²  A type of balance where all the elements of an objeM expand or spiral out from a central point. FOCAL POINT The focus or moT important visual part within a composiCon. ✓ The basic elements and principles can help determine a composiCon’s focal point(E.g. the way the implied line is used, color/value intensity, contraT, etc.)","Triadic,三等分配,模式,The,use,of,three,colors,equally,spaced,around,the,color,wheel,Vibrant,Harmonious,BALANCE,Arranging,elements,in,a,composiCon,so,that,no,one,part,of,a,work,overpowers,or,seem,sheavier,than,any,other,part,Balance,is,a,principle,of,design,that,deals,with,the,visual,weight,within,a,composiCon,Symmetrical,A,balance,that,shows,Tability,usually,centered,in,the,composiCon,VerCcal,A,type,of,symmetrical,balance,that,shows,a,verCcal,orientaCon,Horizontal,A,type,of,symmetrical,balance,that,shows,a,horizontal,orientaCon,Asymmetrical,A,balance,that,is,not,centered,and,not,symmetrical,Radial,A,type,of,balance,where,all,the,elements,of,an,objeM,expand,or,spiral,out,from,a,central,point,FOCAL,POINT,The,focus,or,moT,important,visual,part,within,a,composiCon,The,basic,elements,and,principles,can,help,determine,a,composiCon,s,focal,point,E,g,the,way,the,implied,line,is,used,color,value,intensity,contraT,etc"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"CONTRAST The diﬀerence or opposites of two objeMs, elements, etc. ✓ ContraT is a principle of design that is the arrangement of opposite elements (e.g. light vs. dark colors, rough vs. smooth textures, large vs. small shapes, etc.) in apiece to create visual intereT. INTENSITY The Trength or sharpness of a color due to its degree of freedom from mixture with its complement. ✓ A color’s intensity can be seen at it puriT form or when not mixed with any other color, shade, tone, or Cnt. ✓ Other faMors also play into a color’s intensity. E.g. value cange around a speciﬁc color, texture around a given color, etc. Unit 3: Element and Principles SHAPE A two-dimensional area that is created when a line or contour is closed, when there is a cange in value, or some other form of contraT Shapes help to create: complex drawings and painCng so aﬀeM composiCon o contribute to the balance within a work- All shapes are two-dimensional, meaning that they have only length and width TessellaCon: an arrangement of shapes closely ﬁjed together, especially of polygons in a repeated pajern without gaps or overlapping Geometric (shape): shapes that are usually recognizable by name- Math can be used to ﬁnd informaCon about these shapes- Eg: circle, square, trapezoid, etc Organic (shape): shapes that seem to follow no rules","CONTRAST,di,erence,opposites,two,objeMs,elements,etc,ContraT,principle,design,arrangement,opposite,elements,e,g,light,vs,dark,colors,rough,vs,smooth,textures,large,vs,small,shapes,etc,apiece,create,visual,intereT,INTENSITY,Trength,sharpness,color,due,degree,freedom,mixture,complement,color,intensity,seen,puriT,form,mixed,color,shade,tone,Cnt,faMors,also,play,color,intensity,E,g,value,cange,around,speci,c,color,texture,around,given,color,etc,Unit,Element,Principles,SHAPE,two,dimensional,area,created,line,contour,closed,cange,value,form,contraT,Shapes,help,create,complex,drawings,painCng,eM,composiCon,contribute,balance,within,work,sh