Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"FORM: an element of art that is similar to shape but with the added dimension of depth MOVEMENT A principle of design that uses any element to show an energy, ﬂow, or a feeling that objeMs within a given composiCon are in moCon PATTERN Showing consiTency with colors,lines, values, textures, etc. throughouta composiCon Unit 4: Inner Space and PerspecQve SPACE The visual element that refers to the area between, around, above, below, and within objeMs - Gives artwork its dimension and helps to communicate dynamic composi5on - SomeCmes isn’t aMually within a piece, but the illusion of it is NEGATIVE SPACE Space surrounding shapes or forms in two- and three-dimensional art - As a balance to posiCve space - Oken overlooked - Gives the eye a “place to reT”, increasing the appeal of a composiCon through subtle means POSITIVE SPACE","FORM,element,art,similar,shape,added,dimension,depth,MOVEMENT,principle,design,uses,element,show,energy,ow,feeling,objeMs,within,given,composiCon,moCon,PATTERN,Showing,consiTency,colors,lines,values,textures,etc,throughouta,composiCon,Unit,Inner,Space,PerspecQve,SPACE,visual,element,refers,area,around,within,objeMs,Gives,artwork,dimension,helps,communicate,dynamic,composi,SomeCmes,aMually,within,piece,illusion,NEGATIVE,SPACE,Space,surrounding,shapes,forms,two,three,dimensional,art,balance,posiCve,space,Oken,overlooked,Gives,eye,place,reT,increasing,appeal,composiCon,subtle,means,POSITIVE,SPACE"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Area or part of a painCng’s composiCon that the subjeM occupies - The composiCon’s aMual subjeM majer (the main focus of a work) - Posi5ve space: speciﬁc elements render detail to catB the viewer’s eyeo & should work equally with nega5ve space PROPORTION A principle of art that describes the size, locaCon, or amount of one element to another (or to the whole) in a work - The relaConship between the size of ﬁgures and objeMs within a composiCon - E.g.: The size of an arm in relaCon to the reT of the body, the size of a person in relaCon to the size of a house FORESHORTENING A method of rendering a speciﬁc objeM or ﬁgure in depth. The arCTs records diTorCon that is seen by the eye them an objeM of ﬁgure is viewed at a diTance or unusual angle PERSPECTIVE Developed in the 15th century by the arciteMs Leon BapCTa AlberC (1404-72) and Filippo Brunellesci (1377-1446)- Remained one of the basic principles of WeTern art unCl it was callenged by the ideas of the CubiTs at the Tart of the 20th century Linear Perspec3ve- Deals with the organizaCon of shapes in space Atmosphereic/Aerial PerspecCve- Deals with the atmospheric eﬀeMs ontones and colors ONE POINT PERSPECTIVE","Area,part,painCng,composiCon,subjeM,occupies,composiCon,aMual,subjeM,majer,main,focus,work,Posi,space,speci,c,elements,render,detail,catB,viewer,eyeo,work,equally,nega,space,PROPORTION,principle,art,describes,size,locaCon,amount,one,element,another,whole,work,relaConship,size,gures,objeMs,within,composiCon,E,g,size,arm,relaCon,reT,body,size,person,relaCon,size,house,FORESHORTENING,method,rendering,speci,c,objeM,gure,depth,arCTs,records,diTorCon,seen,eye,objeM,gure,viewed,diTance,unusual,angle,PERSPECTIVE,Developed,th,century,arciteMs,Leon,BapCTa,AlberC,Filippo,Brunellesci,Remained,one,basic,principles,WeTern,art,unCl,callenged,ideas,CubiTs,Tart,th,century,Linear,Perspec,Deals,organizaCon,shapes,space,Atmosphereic,Aerial,PerspecCve,Deals,atmospheric,e,eMs,ontones,colors,ONE,POINT,PERSPECTIVE"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The PerspecCve of a ReMangle/Box - It uses a single vanishing point to draw an objeM- SimpliT form of perspecCve drawing - The front and baf transversal planes always remain parallel to the piMure plane - Only their scale canges as an objeM recedes `into the diTance- Only the receding orthogonal lines cange angles There are two types of conTrucCon lines used in perspecCve drawing TWO POINT PERSPECTIVE - Used in illuTraCons of objeMs whic have been rotated at an angle to the piMure plane - Uses two sets of orthogonal lines and two vanishing points to draw eac objeM - No longer any planes parallel to the piMure plane Unit 5 Vocab Fresco: plaTer wall painCngs ContrappoTo: counterpose, used to describe a body geTure where one leg is infront of the other Columns: A poT or TruMure used to support an arciteMure Arc: a curved arciteMural element used to span an opening Mosaics: The use of small colored objeMs to form a larger image Diptyc: 2 panels of art work that is hinged together Rotunda: arciteMure with a round TruMure & a dome at the top","PerspecCve,ReMangle,Box,uses,single,vanishing,point,draw,objeM,SimpliT,form,perspecCve,drawing,front,baf,transversal,planes,always,remain,parallel,piMure,plane,scale,canges,objeM,recedes,diTance,receding,orthogonal,lines,cange,angles,two,types,conTrucCon,lines,used,perspecCve,drawing,TWO,POINT,PERSPECTIVE,Used,illuTraCons,objeMs,whic,rotated,angle,piMure,plane,Uses,two,sets,orthogonal,lines,two,vanishing,points,draw,eac,objeM,longer,planes,parallel,piMure,plane,Unit,Vocab,Fresco,plaTer,wall,painCngs,ContrappoTo,counterpose,used,describe,body,geTure,one,leg,infront,Columns,poT,TruMure,used,support,arciteMure,Arc,curved,arciteMural,element,used,span,opening,Mosaics,use,small,colored,objeMs,form,larger,image,Diptyc,panels,art,work,hinged,together,Rotunda,arciteMure,round,TruMure,dome,top"
Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Icon: religious symbol Triptyc: 3 panels of art work that is hinged together IlluminaCon: colored illuTraCons containing gold and sliver Cathedral: a large Romanesque or Gothic Tyle curc that houses the cair(cathedra) of the Bishop Cruciform: any design in the shape of a cross Flying Bujress: “ﬂying” arces combined with tower bujresses Vault: The use of the Roman arc with a depth added to it Patron: a person who supports the arts Isocephaly: arranging the heads of ﬁgures at the same level Tempera: a water-based pigment mixed with egg yolk Chiaroscuro: extreme contraT of dark and light values Realism: ajenCon to extreme detail Symbolism: the use of an objeM to represent a meaning other than its own outward appearance Printmaking: the art of using diﬀerent tecniques to make prints Polyptyc: painCng with more then 3 panels hinged together Chateaux: a Frenc caTle or large country house Tenebrism: exaggerated contraT of darks & lights Camera Obscura: a dark box/room with a small opening to let light in Rococo: late Baroque Tyle that is described as prejy or overdone Unit 7 Neoclassicism: (literally means “the New Classic Period”) Napoleon’s intereT in the Classic Greek and Roman periods resulted in his idea,"Icon,religious,symbol,Triptyc,panels,art,work,hinged,together,IlluminaCon,colored,illuTraCons,containing,gold,sliver,Cathedral,large,Romanesque,Gothic,Tyle,curc,houses,cair,cathedra,Bishop,Cruciform,design,shape,cross,Flying,Bujress,ying,arces,combined,tower,bujresses,Vault,use,Roman,arc,depth,added,Patron,person,supports,arts,Isocephaly,arranging,heads,gures,level,Tempera,water,based,pigment,mixed,egg,yolk,Chiaroscuro,extreme,contraT,dark,light,values,Realism,ajenCon,extreme,detail,Symbolism,use,objeM,represent,meaning,outward,appearance,Printmaking,art,using,di,erent,tecniques,make,prints,Polyptyc,painCng,panels,hinged,together,Chateaux,Frenc,caTle,large,country,house,Tenebrism,exaggerated,contraT,darks,lights,Camera,Obscura,dar