Review Guide.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"to “relive” those periods. Allegorical: (Symbols that tell a Tory, a symbolic narraCve) MoT of David’s both told a Tory (moTly hiTorical) and had some type of symbolic meaning or parallel to what was going on in modern day France. RomanQcism: (A movement with a revival of interesCng Medieval Tories and the emoCon of arCsCc elements) NonobjecQve: (Art that has no recognizable subjeM majer,only the use of raw elements)  Some arCTs in RomanCc art used nonrepresentaConal subjeM majer to communicate thee moCon of an idea. RealiX: (A term used to describe an arCT that paint edin the RealiT movement)  The RealiTs emphasize the depicCon of the common, everyday world Photography: (The art of producing images on photosensiCve (light sensiCve) paper)  This tecnology came from the idea of printmaking and how an image can be made by ﬁrT creaCng a mold or Tencil. Impressionism: (A Tyle of painCng that emphasizes momentary eﬀeMs of light on color)  ArCTs seek to create an inTant impression, not a detailed analysis. PoinQllism: (colors that are syTemaCcally applied to canvas with small dots)  Today, we see a similar tecnique in TV screens, computers, and color prinCng. Expressionism: (the communicaCon of Trong personal and emoConal feelings in artwork)  Van Gogh was considered the arCT that began this art movement. PrimiQvism: (less sophisCcated naCve art of any culture)  Gauguin moved to TahiC because he became intereTed in a muc more","relive,periods,Allegorical,Symbols,tell,Tory,symbolic,narraCve,MoT,David,told,Tory,moTly,hiTorical,type,symbolic,meaning,parallel,going,modern,day,France,RomanQcism,movement,revival,interesCng,Medieval,Tories,emoCon,arCsCc,elements,NonobjecQve,Art,recognizable,subjeM,majer,use,raw,elements,arCTs,RomanCc,art,used,nonrepresentaConal,subjeM,majer,communicate,thee,moCon,idea,RealiX,term,used,describe,arCT,paint,edin,RealiT,movement,RealiTs,emphasize,depicCon,common,everyday,world,Photography,art,producing,images,ph