1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q: How are the women presented in myths? List the five main archetypes and explain them.,"Q,women,presented,myths,List,five,main,archetypes,explain"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"A: The Earth Mother – This character is symbolic of fulfilment, abundance, and fertility; offers spiritual and emotional nourishment to those who she contacts; often depicted in earth colours, with large breasts and hips.","Earth,Mother,character,symbolic,fulfilment,abundance,fertility,offers,spiritual,emotional,nourishment,contacts,often,depicted,earth,colours,large,breasts,hips"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Temptress – Characterized by sensuous beauty, she is one whose physical attraction may bring about the hero’s downfall.","Temptress,Characterized,sensuous,beauty,one,whose,physical,attraction,may,bring,hero,downfall"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Platonic Ideal – This source of inspiration often is a physical and spiritual ideal for whom the hero has an intellectual rather than physical attraction.,"Platonic,Ideal,source,inspiration,often,physical,spiritual,ideal,hero,intellectual,rather,physical,attraction"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Unfaithful Wife – This woman, married to a man she sees as dull or distant, is attracted to a more virile or interesting man.","Unfaithful,Wife,woman,married,man,sees,dull,distant,attracted,virile,interesting,man"
