1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q: What cultural anxieties do the Cyclops embody?,"Q,cultural,anxieties,Cyclops,embody"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"A: (Answer may vary) Hospitality (Xenia): In ancient Greece, hospitality, or xenia, was a sacred social custom. In ancient Greece, hosts were expected to provide travellers with food, shelter, and protection, while guests were expected to show gratitude and respect. When Odysseus and his men arrive at Polyphemus' cave, they expect the Cyclops to follow this norm. However, Polyphemus disregards xenia by capturing Odysseus and his men, eating some of them, and imprisoning the rest.","Answer,may,vary,Hospitality,Xenia,ancient,Greece,hospitality,xenia,sacred,social,custom,ancient,Greece,hosts,expected,provide,travellers,food,shelter,protection,guests,expected,show,gratitude,respect,Odysseus,men,arrive,Polyphemus,cave,expect,Cyclops,follow,norm,However,Polyphemus,disregards,xenia,capturing,Odysseus,men,eating,imprisoning,rest"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q: How was the feminist theme expressed through “The Penelopiad” by Margret Atwood?,"Q,feminist,theme,expressed,Penelopiad,Margret,Atwood"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"A: (Answer may vary) The text emphasises Penelope's intelligence and resourcefulness. The text portrays her as a woman who actively engages her mind and uses her wit to navigate challenges. Penelope also expresses empathy and remorse for the hanged maids, shedding light on the injustices faced by marginalised women in the story.","Answer,may,vary,text,emphasises,Penelope,intelligence,resourcefulness,text,portrays,woman,actively,engages,mind,uses,wit,navigate,challenges,Penelope,also,expresses,empathy,remorse,hanged,maids,shedding,light,injustices,faced,marginalised,women,story"
