1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,What does the story reflect of ancient Greek cultural social norms?,"story,reflect,ancient,Greek,cultural,social,norms"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"This story reflects ancient Greek cultural norms such as the importance of purity and virginity for women. It is evident that being a virgin is a highly regarded requirement for becoming one of Athena’s priestesses. Medusa’s tale also reflects the power dynamics between men and women. Even though Poseidon did the unworthy thing, at the end of the day, it was Medusa being punished","story,reflects,ancient,Greek,cultural,norms,importance,purity,virginity,women,evident,virgin,highly,regarded,requirement,becoming,one,Athena,priestesses,Medusa,tale,also,reflects,power,dynamics,men,women,Even,though,Poseidon,unworthy,thing,end,day,Medusa,punished"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,In what ways is Medusa a victim of the patriarchal society?,"ways,Medusa,victim,patriarchal,society"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The ways in which Medusa is portrayed as a victim of patriarchy are represented in the myth when Poseidon rapes her for revenge. Medusa was threatened and raped by Poseidon in Athena’s temple. Even though Poseidon assaulted Medusa, no one","ways,Medusa,portrayed,victim,patriarchy,represented,myth,Poseidon,rapes,revenge,Medusa,threatened,raped,Poseidon,Athena,temple,Even,though,Poseidon,assaulted,Medusa,one"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"blamed him. Instead, Athena blamed Poseidon’s actions on Medusa saying that it was because of her striking appearance that, “diverted men from the path of virtue” (49). In this patriarchal social structure, men’s disreputable actions were blamed upon women.","blamed,Instead,Athena,blamed,Poseidon,actions,Medusa,saying,striking,appearance,diverted,men,path,virtue,patriarchal,social,structure,men,disreputable,actions,blamed,upon,women"
