1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The narrative and events,"narrative,events"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The poem depicts the myth of Perseus slaying Medusa, focusing on the climactic moment when Perseus beheads her. Medusa, with her ""gelid mass of serpents"" representing her deadly, snake-covered head, is asleep. Perseus uses a mirroring shield to view her reflection, avoiding her petrifying gaze. He strikes her, severing her head, and immediately feels an overwhelming, violent urge to destroy more. The narrative hints at Perseus’s triumph, but also reveals the disturbing emotional transformation that accompanies his act.","poem,depicts,myth,Perseus,slaying,Medusa,focusing,climactic,moment,Perseus,beheads,Medusa,gelid,mass,serpents,representing,deadly,snake,covered,head,asleep,Perseus,uses,mirroring,shield,view,reflection,avoiding,petrifying,gaze,strikes,severing,head,immediately,feels,overwhelming,violent,urge,destroy,narrative,hints,Perseus,triumph,also,reveals,disturbing,emotional,transformation,accompanies,act"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The characterization of Perseus,"characterization,Perseus"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Perseus is initially characterized as a heroic figure, executing a dangerous task—killing Medusa, whose gaze turns people to stone. However, his emotions after the act reveal a more complex characterization:","Perseus,initially,characterized,heroic,figure,executing,dangerous,task,killing,Medusa,whose,gaze,turns,people,stone,However,emotions,act,reveal,complex,characterization"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Determination: Perseus successfully accomplishes a difficult task with precision and skill.,"Determination,Perseus,successfully,accomplishes,difficult,task,precision,skill"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Violent Instincts: After beheading Medusa, Perseus experiences a shift in his emotional state. His thirst for destruction (""I thirsted to destroy"") suggests that the act of killing has awakened a darker, more savage side.","Violent,Instincts,beheading,Medusa,Perseus,experiences,shift,emotional,state,thirst,destruction,thirsted,destroy,suggests,act,killing,awakened,darker,savage,side"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Loss of Innocence: The once noble hero becomes consumed by a violent impulse, implying that the act of taking life has fundamentally altered him.","Loss,Innocence,noble,hero,becomes,consumed,violent,impulse,implying,act,taking,life,fundamentally,altered"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"How do literary/poetic devices (diction, rhyme, symbolism, imagery etc.) contribute to this characterization?","literary,poetic,devices,diction,rhyme,symbolism,imagery,etc,contribute,characterization"
1 G9 ENG H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,“Her sleeping head…...of serpents torpidly astir” and “gazing silences and terrored stone”. This kind of imagery alludes to Medusa’s hideous appearance and the tragic outcome of her victims and truly encapsulates the dire tone of the situation that Perseus is in.,"sleeping,head,serpents,torpidly,astir,gazing,silences,terrored,stone,kind,imagery,alludes,Medusa,hideous,appearance,tragic,outcome,victims,truly,encapsulates,dire,tone,situation,Perseus"
