4 IDX G9 ENG H+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Mr. Utterson, a lawyer, learns from his friend Mr. Enfield about a horrible incident, in which a man, Mr. Hyde, trampled a young girl, but paid a large check when threatened by the police.","Mr,Utterson,lawyer,learns,friend,Mr,Enfield,horrible,incident,man,Mr,Hyde,trampled,young,girl,paid,large,check,threatened,police"
4 IDX G9 ENG H+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Chapter 2,Chapter
4 IDX G9 ENG H+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"After returning home, Utterson was troubled by that, one of his clients, Dr. Jekyll, had made a will and left everything to Hyde, rather than his own family. Utterson visits Dr. Lanyon, an old friend of Jekyll. Lanyon had never heard of Mr. Hyde, leaving Utterson more concerned. Utterson then spied on the house where Hyde had trampled the girl. Utterson went to Jekyll’s house, found Jekyll absent, and asked a servant, Poole, who treated My. Hyde almost like a master.","returning,home,Utterson,troubled,one,clients,Dr,Jekyll,made,left,everything,Hyde,rather,family,Utterson,visits,Dr,Lanyon,old,friend,Jekyll,Lanyon,never,heard,Mr,Hyde,leaving,Utterson,concerned,Utterson,spied,house,Hyde,trampled,girl,Utterson,went,Jekyll,house,found,Jekyll,absent,asked,servant,Poole,treated,Hyde,almost,like,master"
