3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Jihad- Struggle in God’s service,"Jihad,Struggle,God,service"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Sharia- Body of law that includes interpretations of the Quran,"Sharia,Body,law,includes,interpretations,Quran"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Q1. What messages, or teachings, did Muhammad spread though Islam?","Q,messages,teachings,Muhammad,spread,though,Islam"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Muhammad rejected traditional gods and left Mecca with his followers to Yathrib on a sacred journey called hijra. He dedicated the temple of Kaaba to Allah and practiced monotheistic. Muslims were required to study the Quan, which contains the sacred word of God, as revealed to Muhammad. It teaches about God’s will and provides a guide to life. Its standards emphasize honesty, generosity, and social justice, such as setting harsh punishments to those who commit crime.","Muhammad,rejected,traditional,gods,left,Mecca,followers,Yathrib,sacred,journey,called,hijra,dedicated,temple,Kaaba,Allah,practiced,monotheistic,Muslims,required,study,Quan,contains,sacred,word,God,revealed,Muhammad,teaches,God,provides,guide,life,standards,emphasize,honesty,generosity,social,justice,setting,harsh,punishments,commit,crime"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q2. How did Muhammad become the prophet of Islam?,"Q,Muhammad,become,prophet,Islam"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Muhammad was known for his honesty in business and was a devoted husband father. He was troubled by the moral ills of society, especially greed. He was about 40 when he heard the voice of voice of the angel Gabriel calling him to become the messenger of God. Muhammad was confused and terrified, but his wife encouraged him to accept the call. Muhammad devoted his life to spreading Islam.","Muhammad,known,honesty,business,devoted,husband,father,troubled,moral,ills,society,especially,greed,heard,voice,voice,angel,Gabriel,calling,become,messenger,God,Muhammad,confused,terrified,wife,encouraged,accept,call,Muhammad,devoted,life,spreading,Islam"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q3. What are the duties required of Muslims?,"Q,duties,required,Muslims"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"All Muslims preform the 5 pillars of Islam. The first is to make a declaration of faith, the second is to pray 5 times daily in a house of worship called mosque. The third is to give charity to the poor, or Almsgiving, and the third is Fasting between dawn and sunset in the month of Ramadan. Lastly, the fifth is to make the hajji, or pilgrimage to Mecca. Additionally, Jihad is a personal duty for Islam, or struggle in God’s service.","Muslims,preform,pillars,Islam,first,make,declaration,faith,second,pray,times,daily,house,worship,called,mosque,third,give,charity,poor,Almsgiving,third,Fasting,dawn,sunset,month,Ramadan,Lastly,fifth,make,hajji,pilgrimage,Mecca,Additionally,Jihad,personal,duty,Islam,struggle,God,service"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q4. How did Islam Affect Women?,"Q,Islam,Affect,Women"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Arab women had limited rights. However, Islam extended rights and protection to women by affirming the spiritual equality of all Muslims. The Quan prohibited the killing of daughters, granted women an inheritance, allowed women to reject a marriage offer as well as equal education to study the Quran. Sill, women’s life and dressing varied to region and class, while still having less statis than men.","Arab,women,limited,rights,However,Islam,extended,rights,protection,women,affirming,spiritual,equality,Muslims,Quan,prohibited,killing,daughters,granted,women,inheritance,allowed,women,reject,marriage,offer,well,equal,education,study,Quran,Sill,women,life,dressing,varied,region,class,still,less,statis,men"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,10.2 Building a Muslim Empire,"Building,Muslim,Empire"
