3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q1. How did Muslims overcome early challenges to Islam?,"Q,Muslims,overcome,early,challenges,Islam"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Abu Bakr was selected to become the first ruler and successor to Muhammad. After battles with wavering tribes, he reunited the Muslims based on their allegiance to Islam. Once united, the Muslims set on a remarkable series of military campaigns. They began by converting the remaining Arab tribes to Islam, which ended the warfare between Arabs and united them under one leader. Under the first four caliphs. The Arabs surprised their neighbors and conquered great portions of the Byzantine empire and defeated the Persians entirely.","Abu,Bakr,selected,become,first,ruler,successor,Muhammad,battles,wavering,tribes,reunited,Muslims,based,allegiance,Islam,united,Muslims,set,remarkable,series,military,campaigns,began,converting,remaining,Arab,tribes,Islam,ended,warfare,Arabs,united,one,leader,first,four,caliphs,Arabs,surprised,neighbors,conquered,great,portions,Byzantine,empire,defeated,Persians,entirely"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q2. Describe differences between Sunni and Shiite Muslims.,"Q,Describe,differences,Sunni,Shiite,Muslims"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Shiites felt that Muhammad had designated his son-in-law, Ali to become his successor, and that the true successors are only descendants of Ali or Muhammad’s daughter, Fatisma. These descendants, called Imams, are divinely inspired religious leaders, who are empowered to interpret the Quran and actions of Muhammad.","Shiites,felt,Muhammad,designated,son,law,Ali,become,successor,true,successors,descendants,Ali,Muhammad,daughter,Fatisma,descendants,called,Imams,divinely,inspired,religious,leaders,empowered,interpret,Quran,actions,Muhammad"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Sunnis felt that any good Muslim could lead the community, since there are no prophets after Muhammad. The majority of Muslims eventually became Sunnis and the successor was decided to be a pious male Muslim from Muhammad’s tribe, called a caliph, a political leader of the religious community.","Sunnis,felt,good,Muslim,could,lead,community,since,prophets,Muhammad,majority,Muslims,eventually,became,Sunnis,successor,decided,pious,male,Muslim,Muhammad,tribe,called,caliph,political,leader,religious,community"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q3. What are three reasons for the success of Muslim conquests?,"Q,three,reasons,success,Muslim,conquests"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The weakness of the Byzantine & Persian empires provided it easy for Muslim to conquer. People welcomed the Arabs as liberators from their harsh rule. The Arab’s bold efficient fighting methods also lead its way to success. (ex. War of Yarmuk). The Muslim also formed treaties and alliances with Spain to maintain powers. Share cultures and traditions as well as standing in the same side against enemies.,"weakness,Byzantine,Persian,empires,provided,easy,Muslim,conquer,People,welcomed,Arabs,liberators,harsh,rule,Arab,bold,efficient,fighting,methods,also,lead,way,success,ex,War,Yarmuk,Muslim,also,formed,treaties,alliances,Spain,maintain,powers,Share,cultures,traditions,well,standing,side,enemies"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q4. How did Islam become a more universal faith?,"Q,Islam,become,universal,faith"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"As Muslim civilization developed, many Jews & Christians played key roles as officials, doctors and translators. Muslim leaders wisely prohibited looting and destruction of conquered lands, ensuring continued wealth and prosperity for the empire in form of thrive and advantages. However, many were drawn to Islam’s simple and direct messages for them to see its triumph as a sign of God’s favor. Most nomadic in North Africa and Central Asia chose Islam immediately. Islam have no religious hierarchy (class of priests). It emphasizes the equality of all believers, regardless of race, gender, or wealth.","Muslim,civilization,developed,many,Jews,Christians,played,key,roles,officials,doctors,translators,Muslim,leaders,wisely,prohibited,looting,destruction,conquered,lands,ensuring,continued,wealth,prosperity,empire,form,thrive,advantages,However,many,drawn,Islam,simple,direct,messages,see,triumph,sign,God,favor,nomadic,North,Africa,Central,Asia,chose,Islam,immediately,Islam,religious,hierarchy,class,priests,emphasizes,equality,believers,regardless,race,gender,wealth"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Q5. What caused the Abbasid dynasty to decline?,"Q,caused,Abbasid,dynasty,decline"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Abbasids never ruled Spain and Starting about 850, their control over the rest of Muslim empire fragmented. As Caliph’s powers faded in some regions, Shiite rulers came to power with a series of invasion.","Abbasids,never,ruled,Spain,Starting,control,rest,Muslim,empire,fragmented,Caliph,powers,faded,regions,Shiite,rulers,came,power,series,invasion"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1216, Genghis Kran led the Mongols out of the Central Asia across southwest Asia, returning again and again. In 1258, Hulagu, the great grandson of Genghis, burned and looted Baghdad, killing the last Abbasid Caliph. In the late 1300s, another Mongol leader, Timur the lame, or Tamerlane, led his armies to the Middle East. His ambitions led him to conquered Muslim and non-Muslim lands, ending the Abbasid dynasty.","Genghis,Kran,led,Mongols,Central,Asia,across,southwest,Asia,returning,Hulagu,great,grandson,Genghis,burned,looted,Baghdad,killing,last,Abbasid,Caliph,late,another,Mongol,leader,Timur,lame,Tamerlane,led,armies,Middle,East,ambitions,led,conquered,Muslim,non,Muslim,lands,ending,Abbasid,dynasty"
3 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In Egypt, independent dynasties ruled states that were part of an unified empire.","Egypt,independent,dynasties,ruled,states,part,unified,empire"
