5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"NOTE: This is an official document by Indexademics. Unless otherwise stated, this document may not be accredited to individuals or groups other than the club IDX, nor should this document be distributed, sold, or modified for personal use in any way.","NOTE,official,document,Indexademics,Unless,otherwise,stated,document,may,accredited,individuals,groups,club,IDX,document,distributed,sold,modified,personal,use,way"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,12.1 Two Golden Ages of China,"Two,Golden,Ages,China"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Tang Dynasty Reunifies China,"Tang,Dynasty,Reunifies,China"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"After the Han dynasty collapsed in 220, China remained divided for nearly 400 years. During the brief period of the Sui dynasty (589-618), China was unified by the South and North, but the glory was not restored until the emergence of the Tang dynasty in 618.","Han,dynasty,collapsed,China,remained,divided,nearly,years,brief,period,Sui,dynasty,China,unified,South,North,glory,restored,emergence,Tang,dynasty"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Tang Build an Empire,"Tang,Build,Empire"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The first emperor of the Tang dynasty, Li Yuan, was originally a general under the Sui dynasty. Sought the throne encouraged by his ambitious 16-year-old son, Li Shimin.","first,emperor,Tang,dynasty,Li,Yuan,originally,general,Sui,dynasty,Sought,throne,encouraged,ambitious,year,old,son,Li,Shimin"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"After Li Yuan ruled the Tang dynasty for 8 years, Li Shimin compelled his father to give up the throne, and having Li Shimin ruling the dynasty. Then, Li Shimin took the name Tang Taizong.","Li,Yuan,ruled,Tang,dynasty,years,Li,Shimin,compelled,father,give,throne,Li,Shimin,ruling,dynasty,Li,Shimin,took,name,Tang,Taizong"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Li Shimin was a brilliant general, government reformer, historian and master of calligraphy.","Li,Shimin,brilliant,general,government,reformer,historian,master,calligraphy"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Li Shimin expanded the territories into Central Asia and forced neighboring lands to become tributary states.,"Li,Shimin,expanded,territories,Central,Asia,forced,neighboring,lands,become,tributary,states"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Spread culture to neighboring countries.,"Spread,culture,neighboring,countries"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Government and Economy Grow,"Government,Economy,Grow"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Tang Rulers restored the Han bureaucracy & enlarged the civil system.,"Tang,Rulers,restored,Han,bureaucracy,enlarged,civil,system"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Allowed the government to recruit more talented people.,"Allowed,government,recruit,talented,people"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trained in Confucian philosophy.,"Trained,Confucian,philosophy"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Develop schools to prepare for the exams.,"Develop,schools,prepare,exams"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Created a new law code.,"Created,new,law,code"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Instituted system of land reform.,"Instituted,system,land,reform"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Redistributed land held by local authorities/large agricultural holdings allow peasants to get a fraction of land.,"Redistributed,land,held,local,authorities,large,agricultural,holdings,allow,peasants,get,fraction,land"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Strengthened central power by weakening the landowners’ economic power.,"Strengthened,central,power,weakening,landowners,economic,power"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Increased government revenue, more peasants pay tax.","Increased,government,revenue,peasants,pay,tax"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Tang Dynasty Declines,"Tang,Dynasty,Declines"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Tang dynasty eventually lost territories in Central Asia and to the Arabs.,"Tang,dynasty,eventually,lost,territories,Central,Asia,Arabs"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 907, a rebellion occurred and overthrew the Tang dynasty.","rebellion,occurred,overthrew,Tang,dynasty"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Song Dynasty,"Song,Dynasty"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 960, a scholarly general named Zhao Kuangyin ruled China and formed the Song dynasty.","scholarly,general,named,Zhao,Kuangyin,ruled,China,formed,Song,dynasty"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Lasted for 319 years.,"Lasted,years"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Gained fewer territories than the Tang dynasty.,"Gained,fewer,territories,Tang,dynasty"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Faced constant threats from invaders from the north.,"Faced,constant,threats,invaders,north"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In the early 1100s, the Song dynasty retreated to the south of the Huang River.","early,Song,dynasty,retreated,south,Huang,River"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Eventually, in the late 1200s, Song was overthrown by the Mongols.","Eventually,late,Song,overthrown,Mongols"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Song dynasty developed the economy and culture.,"Song,dynasty,developed,economy,culture"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"People created new farming methods during the Song dynasty. Another type of rice was imported from Southeast Asia, which allowed people to harvest more crops.","People,created,new,farming,methods,Song,dynasty,Another,type,rice,imported,Southeast,Asia,allowed,people,harvest,crops"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The more crops allowed people to use it to sell for money, at the same time enhanced the economy and provide surplus resources to let people discover other matters, such as arts and commerce.","crops,allowed,people,use,sell,money,time,enhanced,economy,provide,surplus,resources,let,people,discover,matters,arts,commerce"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Song dynasty constructed canals.,"Song,dynasty,constructed,canals"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"E.g. the Grand Canal, transported grain from south to northern China.","E,g,Grand,Canal,transported,grain,south,northern,China"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Foreign Trade flourished. Trade routes with India, Persia, Arabia, etc., had opened.","Foreign,Trade,flourished,Trade,routes,India,Persia,Arabia,etc,opened"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,China’s Ordered Society,"China,Ordered,Society"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Gentry Value and Education,"Gentry,Value,Education"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Gentry: Wealthy landowning class,"Gentry,Wealthy,landowning,class"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Most scholar-officials came from the gentry. They studied Confucian classics for years to pass the civil service exam.,"scholar,officials,came,gentry,studied,Confucian,classics,years,pass,civil,service,exam"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Gentry often served as allies of the emperor’s officials.,"Gentry,often,served,allies,emperor,officials"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Gentry valued learning more than physical labor. Supported the revival of Confucian thoughts. Take Confucian officials as the ones that are wise and clever in the society.,"Gentry,valued,learning,physical,labor,Supported,revival,Confucian,thoughts,Take,Confucian,officials,ones,wise,clever,society"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Peasants Work the Land,"Peasants,Work,Land"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Many of the Chinese depended on crops to live their life, but some of them made small handicrafts and sold them to increase their earning.","Many,Chinese,depended,crops,live,life,made,small,handicrafts,sold,increase,earning"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"People lived in small villages, where they depended on each other rather than believing in the government.","People,lived,small,villages,depended,rather,believing,government"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"When arguments took place, a village leader and a council of elders would come to solve the problem.","arguments,took,place,village,leader,council,elders,would,come,solve,problem"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Merchants Have Lowest Status,"Merchants,Lowest,Status"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"According to Confucian traditions, merchants had a lower social status than peasants since their wealth came from the labor of others.","According,Confucian,traditions,merchants,lower,social,status,peasants,since,wealth,came,labor,others"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Merchants needed to be educated to enter the gentry.,"Merchants,needed,educated,enter,gentry"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Status of Women,"Status,Women"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Women had a relatively high status in the Tang and early Song dynasties compared to later periods.,"Women,relatively,high,status,Tang,early,Song,dynasties,compared,later,periods"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Women in families tended to run family affairs, such as managing servants and family finances.","Women,families,tended,run,family,affairs,managing,servants,family,finances"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"A male’s status is still higher than a female’s. When women got married to men, they could not keep their dowry and could never remarry.","male,status,still,higher,female,women,got,married,men,could,keep,dowry,could,never,remarry"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The tradition of Foot Binding emerged in the late Song dynasty. Acted as a symbol of nobility and beauty.,"tradition,Foot,Binding,emerged,late,Song,dynasty,Acted,symbol,nobility,beauty"
5 IDX G9 HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Tang and Song Dynasties Develop a Rich Culture,"Tang,Song,Dynasties,Develop,Rich,Culture"
