7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,6.3 Periodic Trends,"Periodic,Trends"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Many properties of the elements change in a predictable way as you move through the period table, and these systematic variations are called periodic trends","Many,properties,elements,change,predictable,way,move,period,table,systematic,variations,called,periodic,trends"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,I. Trends in Atomic Size,"Trends,Atomic,Size"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The atomic radius is one-half of the distance between the nuclei of two atoms of the same element when the atoms are joined,"atomic,radius,one,half,distance,nuclei,two,atoms,element,atoms,joined"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The atomic radius is often measured in picometers (pm).,"atomic,radius,often,measured,picometers,pm"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The attraction force between electrons and nucleus will affect many atom’s properties,"attraction,force,electrons,nucleus,affect,many,atom,properties"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trend 1: Atoms get larger going down a group.,"Trend,Atoms,get,larger,going,group"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Going down a group = more energy levels, attraction decrease = outmost electrons go further, size increase","Going,group,energy,levels,attraction,decrease,outmost,electrons,go,size,increase"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trend 2: Atoms get smaller moving from left to right across each period.,"Trend,Atoms,get,smaller,moving,left,right,across,period"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Moving from left to right = same energy level, more protons, attraction increase = outmost electrons closer, atom size decrease","Moving,left,right,energy,level,protons,attraction,increase,outmost,electrons,closer,atom,size,decrease"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,II. Trend for Ionic Size,"II,Trend,Ionic,Size"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,An ion is an atom or group of atoms that has a positive or negative charge,"ion,atom,group,atoms,positive,negative,charge"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,An ion with a positive charge is called a cation (metal easy to lose electrons),"ion,positive,charge,called,cation,metal,easy,lose,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,An ion with a negative charge is called an anion (nonmetal easy to gain electron),"ion,negative,charge,called,anion,nonmetal,easy,gain,electron"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Octet rule: Atoms tend to gain, lose, or share electrons in order to acquire a full set of valence electrons","Octet,rule,Atoms,tend,gain,lose,share,electrons,order,acquire,full,set,valence,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"For most energy levels, there are 8 valence electrons in a full set of valence electrons --- 2 in s orbital and 6 in p orbitals","energy,levels,valence,electrons,full,set,valence,electrons,orbital,p,orbitals"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"An exception for the first energy level, which is full with only 2 electrons","exception,first,energy,level,full,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The elements on the right side of the periodic table tend to gain electrons – or become anions – in order to acquire a complete set of valence electrons (being stable),"elements,right,side,periodic,table,tend,gain,electrons,become,anions,order,acquire,complete,set,valence,electrons,stable"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The elements on the left side of the periodic table tend to lose electrons – or become cations – in order to acquire a complete set of valence electrons (being stable),"elements,left,side,periodic,table,tend,lose,electrons,become,cations,order,acquire,complete,set,valence,electrons,stable"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Noble gases neither gain nor lose electrons,"Noble,gases,neither,gain,lose,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Positive Ions (lose electrons) become smaller, because the repulsion between electrons is reduced, radius of a cation is smaller than an atom","Positive,Ions,lose,electrons,become,smaller,repulsion,electrons,reduced,radius,cation,smaller,atom"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Negative Ions (gain electrons) become larger, because the repulsion between electrons is increased, radius of an anion is larger than an atom","Negative,Ions,gain,electrons,become,larger,repulsion,electrons,increased,radius,anion,larger,atom"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trend 1: Ions get larger going down a group,"Trend,Ions,get,larger,going,group"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trend 2: Ions get smaller from left to right,"Trend,Ions,get,smaller,left,right"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The anions in same period and cation of next period have same number of electrons but proton number is increasing in nucleus, thus the attraction force increases and ion sized decreases","anions,period,cation,next,period,number,electrons,proton,number,increasing,nucleus,thus,attraction,force,increases,ion,sized,decreases"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Trend 3: For same elements, the one with less electrons (more positive or less negative) is smaller","Trend,elements,one,less,electrons,positive,less,negative,smaller"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,III. Trend for Ionization Energy,"III,Trend,Ionization,Energy"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,An atom’s ionization energy (I) is the energy needed to remove one of its electrons,"atom,ionization,energy,energy,needed,remove,one,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Atoms with high I hold onto their electrons tightly, whereas atoms with low I are more likely to lose outmost electrons","Atoms,high,hold,onto,electrons,tightly,whereas,atoms,low,likely,lose,outmost,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Trend 1: Ionization energies decreases as you move down a group (more energy level, far away from the nucleus)","Trend,Ionization,energies,decreases,move,group,energy,level,far,away,nucleus"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trend 2: Ionization energies increases as you move from left to right across a period (ions get smaller so nearer to the nucleus so more energy is required to remove electrons),"Trend,Ionization,energies,increases,move,left,right,across,period,ions,get,smaller,nearer,nucleus,energy,required,remove,electrons"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Ionization energy trends are exactly opposite of the trends for atomic radius, and radius is inversely proportional to attraction while ionization energy is proportional to attraction","Ionization,energy,trends,exactly,opposite,trends,atomic,radius,radius,inversely,proportional,attraction,ionization,energy,proportional,attraction"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The successive ionization energies are the energies required to remove electron beyond the first electron,"successive,ionization,energies,energies,required,remove,electron,beyond,first,electron"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Trend 3: the ionization energies increase for every electron removed,"Trend,ionization,energies,increase,every,electron,removed"
7 IDX G9 CHEM S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"An atom holds the electrons in its noble gas inner core much more strongly than it holds its valence electrons, so there is a large increase when the atom begins to lose the inner electron","atom,holds,electrons,noble,gas,inner,core,much,strongly,holds,valence,electrons,large,increase,atom,begins,lose,inner,electron"
