7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Erosion: the process by which water dislodges, dissolves, or removes weathered surface material","Erosion,process,water,dislodges,dissolves,removes,weathered,surface,material"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Deposition: when the transported material is laid down,"Deposition,transported,material,laid"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Hydraulic action: a type or erosive work performed by flowing water alone,"Hydraulic,action,type,erosive,work,performed,flowing,water,alone"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Abrasion: debris eroding the streambed. like sandpaper,"Abrasion,debris,eroding,streambed,like,sandpaper"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Channel incision: process where streams deepen their channel,"Channel,incision,process,streams,deepen,channel"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Headward erosion: process where streams lengthen their channels upstream,"Headward,erosion,process,streams,lengthen,channels,upstream"
