7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Capacity: total possible sediment load that it can transport. directly related to discharge,"Capacity,total,possible,sediment,load,transport,directly,related,discharge"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Degradation: channel erosion,"Degradation,channel,erosion"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Aggradation: stream channel building up through deposition. opposite of degradation,"Aggradation,stream,channel,building,deposition,opposite,degradation"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Braided stream: excess sediment turning a stream into interconnected channels. occurs when 	reduced discharge lowers its transporting ability or if a landslide occurs upstream. 	commonly occur in glacial environments.,"Braided,stream,excess,sediment,turning,stream,interconnected,channels,occurs,reduced,discharge,lowers,transporting,ability,landslide,occurs,upstream,commonly,occur,glacial,environments"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Meandering stream: where streams develop a more sinuous form. tendency to meander is 	evidence of a river system's ability to find the path of least effort towards a balance between 	order and disorder,"Meandering,stream,streams,develop,sinuous,form,tendency,meander,evidence,river,system,ability,find,path,least,effort,towards,balance,order,disorder"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Undercut bank (cutbank): place that undergoes the greatest erosive action (scouring),"Undercut,bank,cutbank,place,undergoes,greatest,erosive,action,scouring"
