7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"River Rejuvenation: - when tectonic uplift changes the elevation of a graded stream relative to its base level, which increases the stream gradient and stimulates erosional activity. The river gains energy and actively returns to downcutting, which can eventually form entrenched meanders","River,Rejuvenation,tectonic,uplift,changes,elevation,graded,stream,relative,base,level,increases,stream,gradient,stimulates,erosional,activity,river,gains,energy,actively,returns,downcutting,eventually,form,entrenched,meanders"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Antecedent Stream: - a rejuvenated river that downcuts at the same rate as the tectonic uplift, so it maintains its course","Antecedent,Stream,rejuvenated,river,downcuts,rate,tectonic,uplift,maintains,course"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Nickpoint (also spelled as knickpoint): - the point of interruption when the longitudinal profile of a stream contains an abrupt change in gradient (e.g. at a waterfall). Temporary blockages such as a landslide also count. Relatively temporary and mobile feature. Nickpoints can migrate upstream due to headward erosion,"Nickpoint,also,spelled,knickpoint,point,interruption,longitudinal,profile,stream,contains,abrupt,change,gradient,e,g,waterfall,Temporary,blockages,landslide,also,count,Relatively,temporary,mobile,feature,Nickpoints,migrate,upstream,due,headward,erosion"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Alluvium: - the general term for the unconsolidated clay, silt, sand, gravel, and mineral fragments deposited by running water; may accumulate as sorted or unsorted sediment","Alluvium,general,term,unconsolidated,clay,silt,sand,gravel,mineral,fragments,deposited,running,water,may,accumulate,sorted,unsorted,sediment"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Fluvial Deposition: - occurs when a stream deposits alluvium, thereby creating depositional landforms, such as bars, floodplains, terraces, and deltas","Fluvial,Deposition,occurs,stream,deposits,alluvium,thereby,creating,depositional,landforms,bars,floodplains,terraces,deltas"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Floodplain: - the flat, low-lying area adjacent to a channel and subjected to recurrent flooding; layered with alluvial deposits that mask the underlying rock","Floodplain,flat,low,lying,area,adjacent,channel,subjected,recurrent,flooding,layered,alluvial,deposits,mask,underlying,rock"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Natural Levees: - low ridges of coarse sediment on either bank of some rivers, mostly composed of coarser, sand-sized particles that are deposited first along the banks as rivers overflow their banks (these larger particles are dropped first because of their size)","Natural,Levees,low,ridges,coarse,sediment,either,bank,rivers,mostly,composed,coarser,sand,sized,particles,deposited,first,along,banks,rivers,overflow,banks,larger,particles,dropped,first,size"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Riparian Marshes (Backswamps): - wetlands that often form in the poorly drained fine sediments deposited by overbank flows,"Riparian,Marshes,Backswamps,wetlands,often,form,poorly,drained,fine,sediments,deposited,overbank,flows"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Yazoo Streams (yazoo tributaries): - flow parallel to the main river but are blocked from joining it by the presence of natural levees,"Yazoo,Streams,yazoo,tributaries,flow,parallel,main,river,blocked,joining,presence,natural,levees"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Alluvial Terraces: - produced by entrenchment of a river into its own floodplain due to tectonic uplift, look like topographic steps above the river. Generally appear paired at similar elevations on the sides of the valley","Alluvial,Terraces,produced,entrenchment,river,floodplain,due,tectonic,uplift,look,like,topographic,steps,river,Generally,appear,paired,similar,elevations,sides,valley"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Alluvial Fans: - in arid and semiarid climates, prominent cone-shaped/fan-shaped deposits of fluvial sediments, commonly occurring at the mouth of a canyon, produced when flowing water abruptly loses velocity as it leaves the canyon. The sediments in an alluvial fan are naturally sorted by size, with the coarsest materials deposited near the mouth of the canyon and the finest clays carried all the way to the valley floor","Alluvial,Fans,arid,semiarid,climates,prominent,cone,shaped,fan,shaped,deposits,fluvial,sediments,commonly,occurring,mouth,canyon,produced,flowing,water,abruptly,loses,velocity,leaves,canyon,sediments,alluvial,fan,naturally,sorted,size,coarsest,materials,deposited,near,mouth,canyon,finest,clays,carried,way,valley,floor"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Bajada: - formed by individual alluvial fans that coalesce into one sloping surface,"Bajada,formed,individual,alluvial,fans,coalesce,one,sloping,surface"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Playa: - salt crusts left behind on the desert floor after water evaporates,"Playa,salt,crusts,left,behind,desert,floor,water,evaporates"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Delta: - the level or nearly level depositional plain that forms at the mouth of a river,"Delta,level,nearly,level,depositional,plain,forms,mouth,river"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Distributaries: - channels running through the delta that divide into smaller courses (think opposite of tributaries),"Distributaries,channels,running,delta,divide,smaller,courses,think,opposite,tributaries"
7 IDX G9 GEO H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Estuary: - the body of water at a river’s mouth where freshwater flow encounters seawater,"Estuary,body,water,river,mouth,freshwater,flow,encounters,seawater"
