7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Background to the Reformation,"Background,Reformation"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Northern Europeans faced life uncertainty. Fixed medieval economies shifted to urban, market - based ones with unequal wealth distribution.","Northern,Europeans,faced,life,uncertainty,Fixed,medieval,economies,shifted,urban,market,based,ones,unequal,wealth,distribution"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Renaissance humanist ideas spread via the printing press. Ideas like classical education and social reform took root, leading people to question the Church.","Renaissance,humanist,ideas,spread,via,printing,press,Ideas,like,classical,education,social,reform,took,root,leading,people,question,Church"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Church abuses were rife. Popes engaged in political power struggles, led lavish lives, and increased service fees. Some clergy sold indulgences, which were originally for good deeds but by the late 1400s could be bought with money.","Church,abuses,rife,Popes,engaged,political,power,struggles,led,lavish,lives,increased,service,fees,clergy,sold,indulgences,originally,good,deeds,late,could,bought,money"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Early revolts against the Church occurred. John Wycliffe in 1300s England and Jan Hus in what's now the Czech Republic protested Church practices.,"Early,revolts,Church,occurred,John,Wycliffe,England,Jan,Hus,Czech,Republic,protested,Church,practices"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Martin Luther: Catalyst of Change,"Martin,Luther,Catalyst,Change"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1517, Johann Tetzel's sale of indulgences to fund St. Peter's Cathedral rebuilding enraged Luther. Tetzel claimed indulgences guaranteed heaven for buyers and their dead relatives.","Johann,Tetzel,sale,indulgences,fund,St,Peter,Cathedral,rebuilding,enraged,Luther,Tetzel,claimed,indulgences,guaranteed,heaven,buyers,dead,relatives"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Luther wrote the 95 Theses against indulgences. Argued they had no basis in the Bible, the pope had no authority over purgatory, and salvation was through faith.","Luther,wrote,Theses,indulgences,Argued,basis,Bible,pope,authority,purgatory,salvation,faith"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Copies of the 95 Theses spread rapidly across Europe, sparking debate. Luther refused to recant when the Church demanded it.","Copies,Theses,spread,rapidly,across,Europe,sparking,debate,Luther,refused,recant,Church,demanded"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Luther developed radical doctrines. Urged Christians to reject Rome's authority, believed the Church could be reformed by secular authorities.","Luther,developed,radical,doctrines,Urged,Christians,reject,Rome,authority,believed,Church,could,reformed,secular,authorities"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1521, Pope Leo X excommunicated Luther. Emperor Charles V summoned him to the Diet of Worms. Luther refused to give up his writings, was declared an outlaw.","Pope,Leo,X,excommunicated,Luther,Emperor,Charles,V,summoned,Diet,Worms,Luther,refused,give,writings,declared,outlaw"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Luther's Teachings,"Luther,Teachings"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Salvation by faith alone. All Christians had equal access to God through faith and the Bible.,"Salvation,faith,alone,Christians,equal,access,God,faith,Bible"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Rejected some sacraments. Believed rituals couldn't erase sin; only God could.,"Rejected,sacraments,Believed,rituals,erase,sin,God,could"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Bible as the sole source of truth. Luther translated parts of the Bible into German and wanted everyone to be able to read it.,"Bible,sole,source,truth,Luther,translated,parts,Bible,German,wanted,everyone,able,read"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Simplified church practices. Banned indulgences, confession, pilgrimages, and prayers to saints. Simplified the mass and emphasized sermons. Allowed clergy to marry.","Simplified,church,practices,Banned,indulgences,confession,pilgrimages,prayers,saints,Simplified,mass,emphasized,sermons,Allowed,clergy,marry"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Luther's Ideas Spread,"Luther,Ideas,Spread"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Printing presses spread Luther's writings in Germany and Scandinavia.,"Printing,presses,spread,Luther,writings,Germany,Scandinavia"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Many clergy saw his reforms as a solution to Church corruption.,"Many,clergy,saw,reforms,solution,Church,corruption"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Some German princes embraced Lutheranism for self - serving reasons. To break free from Church and imperial rule, seize Church property, or due to national loyalty.","German,princes,embraced,Lutheranism,self,serving,reasons,break,free,Church,imperial,rule,seize,Church,property,due,national,loyalty"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Peasants' Revolt in 1524 was inspired by Luther's ideas. Peasants hoped for social and economic change, like an end to serfdom. Luther denounced the revolt as it grew violent, and nobles suppressed it.","Peasants,Revolt,inspired,Luther,ideas,Peasants,hoped,social,economic,change,like,end,serfdom,Luther,denounced,revolt,grew,violent,nobles,suppressed"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Peace of Augsburg in 1555 allowed German princes to choose between Catholicism and Lutheranism. Most northern states chose Lutheranism, southern states remained Catholic.","Peace,Augsburg,allowed,German,princes,choose,Catholicism,Lutheranism,northern,states,chose,Lutheranism,southern,states,remained,Catholic"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Switzerland's Reformation,"Switzerland,Reformation"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Ulrich Zwingli in Zurich stressed the importance of the Bible and rejected elaborate rituals.,"Ulrich,Zwingli,Zurich,stressed,importance,Bible,rejected,elaborate,rituals"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"John Calvin, born in France, published a book in 1536. Set forth his beliefs, including predestination (God had long ago determined who would be saved).","John,Calvin,born,France,published,book,Set,forth,beliefs,including,predestination,God,long,ago,determined,would,saved"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1541, Calvin led Geneva. Set up a theocracy run by church leaders. Calvinists emphasized hard work, discipline, thrift, honesty, and morality.","Calvin,led,Geneva,Set,theocracy,run,church,leaders,Calvinists,emphasized,hard,work,discipline,thrift,honesty,morality"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Calvinism spread across Europe. It led to religious wars in Germany, France, the Netherlands, England, and Scotland.","Calvinism,spread,across,Europe,led,religious,wars,Germany,France,Netherlands,England,Scotland"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Section 13.4: Reformation Ideas Spread,"Section,Reformation,Ideas,Spread"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,An Explosion of Protestant Sects,"Explosion,Protestant,Sects"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"As the Reformation continued, numerous new Protestant sects emerged.","Reformation,continued,numerous,new,Protestant,sects,emerged"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Anabaptists were a radical group. Rejected infant baptism, arguing infants were too young to understand the Christian faith.","Anabaptists,radical,group,Rejected,infant,baptism,arguing,infants,young,understand,Christian,faith"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Some Anabaptist sects sought social change. Wanted to abolish private property or speed up God's judgment day.,"Anabaptist,sects,sought,social,change,Wanted,abolish,private,property,speed,God,judgment,day"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Most Anabaptists were peaceful. Called for religious toleration and separation of church and state. Influenced Protestant thinking; Baptists, Mennonites, and Amish trace their roots to them.","Anabaptists,peaceful,Called,religious,toleration,separation,church,state,Influenced,Protestant,thinking,Baptists,Mennonites,Amish,trace,roots"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The English Reformation,"English,Reformation"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In the 1300s, John Wycliffe called for Church reform in England. By the 1520s, some clergy explored Protestant ideas.","John,Wycliffe,called,Church,reform,England,clergy,explored,Protestant,ideas"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Henry VIII initially opposed Protestantism. The pope gave him the title ""Defender of the Faith"" for denouncing Luther.","Henry,VIII,initially,opposed,Protestantism,pope,gave,title,Defender,Faith,denouncing,Luther"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1527, Henry wanted an annulment of his marriage to Catherine of Aragon. He wanted to marry Anne Boleyn to have a male heir. The pope refused, not wanting to offend Charles V.","Henry,wanted,annulment,marriage,Catherine,Aragon,wanted,marry,Anne,Boleyn,male,heir,pope,refused,wanting,offend,Charles,V"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Henry broke with the Church. Guided by Thomas Cromwell, Parliament passed laws taking the English church from papal control. Henry appointed Thomas Cranmer as archbishop.","Henry,broke,Church,Guided,Thomas,Cromwell,Parliament,passed,laws,taking,English,church,papal,control,Henry,appointed,Thomas,Cranmer,archbishop"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1534, Parliament passed the Act of Supremacy, making Henry the head of the Church of England. Loyal Catholics who refused to accept it, like Sir Thomas More, were executed.","Parliament,passed,Act,Supremacy,making,Henry,head,Church,England,Loyal,Catholics,refused,accept,like,Sir,Thomas,executed"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Henry closed Catholic convents and monasteries between 1536 - 1540. Confiscated their lands and wealth, and granted some to nobles to secure support for the Anglican Church.","Henry,closed,Catholic,convents,monasteries,Confiscated,lands,wealth,granted,nobles,secure,support,Anglican,Church"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"After Henry's death, Edward VI became king. He and his advisors were Protestants. Parliament passed laws for Protestant reforms, and Cranmer drew up the Protestant Book of Common Prayer.","Henry,death,Edward,VI,became,king,advisors,Protestants,Parliament,passed,laws,Protestant,reforms,Cranmer,drew,Protestant,Book,Common,Prayer"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Mary Tudor became queen after Edward's death. She tried to restore Catholicism. Hundreds of Protestants, including Cranmer, were burned at the stake.","Mary,Tudor,became,queen,Edward,death,tried,restore,Catholicism,Hundreds,Protestants,including,Cranmer,burned,stake"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Elizabeth I became queen in 1558. Her Elizabethan Settlement was a compromise between Protestant and Catholic practices. Preserved Catholic rituals, reaffirmed the monarch's spiritual authority, and restored a version of the Book of Common Prayer.","Elizabeth,became,queen,Elizabethan,Settlement,compromise,Protestant,Catholic,practices,Preserved,Catholic,rituals,reaffirmed,monarch,spiritual,authority,restored,version,Book,Common,Prayer"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Catholic Reformation,"Catholic,Reformation"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Led by Pope Paul III, the Catholic Reformation aimed to revive the Church's moral authority and counter the Protestant tide.","Led,Pope,Paul,III,Catholic,Reformation,aimed,revive,Church,moral,authority,counter,Protestant,tide"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The Council of Trent, called in 1545, met for almost 20 years. Reaffirmed traditional Catholic views, declared salvation through faith and good works, and took steps to end Church abuses.","Council,Trent,called,met,almost,years,Reaffirmed,traditional,Catholic,views,declared,salvation,faith,good,works,took,steps,end,Church,abuses"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Pope Paul strengthened the Inquisition. It used secret testimony, torture, and execution to fight Protestantism and created the Index of Forbidden Books.","Pope,Paul,strengthened,Inquisition,used,secret,testimony,torture,execution,fight,Protestantism,created,Index,Forbidden,Books"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1540, the Jesuits (Society of Jesus) were founded by Ignatius of Loyola. They had strict spiritual and moral discipline, and their members became advisors to Catholic rulers, set up schools, and spread the Catholic faith worldwide.","Jesuits,Society,Jesus,founded,Ignatius,Loyola,strict,spiritual,moral,discipline,members,became,advisors,Catholic,rulers,set,schools,spread,Catholic,faith,worldwide"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Teresa of Avila, a Spanish nun, reformed convents and monasteries. Her spiritual writings were important, and she was canonized.","Teresa,Avila,Spanish,nun,reformed,convents,monasteries,spiritual,writings,important,canonized"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"By 1600, the Catholic Reformation had reduced Church abuses, brought back some Protestant converts, but Protestantism still had a major foothold in Europe.","Catholic,Reformation,reduced,Church,abuses,brought,back,Protestant,converts,Protestantism,still,major,foothold,Europe"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Widespread Persecution,"Widespread,Persecution"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"During the Reformation, both Catholics and Protestants persecuted radical sects, witches, and Jews.","Reformation,Catholics,Protestants,persecuted,radical,sects,witches,Jews"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Witch hunts occurred between 1450 - 1750. Tens of thousands of mostly women were accused of being witches, seen as anti - Christian. Persecution declined with the end of religious wars.","Witch,hunts,occurred,Tens,thousands,mostly,women,accused,witches,seen,anti,Christian,Persecution,declined,end,religious,wars"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Jews faced increasing restrictions. Venice ordered them to live in ghettos in 1516. Luther called for their expulsion when they didn't convert. Popes and emperors also imposed restrictions, leading many Jews to migrate.","Jews,faced,increasing,restrictions,Venice,ordered,live,ghettos,Luther,called,expulsion,convert,Popes,emperors,also,imposed,restrictions,leading,many,Jews,migrate"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Section 13.5: The Scientific Revolution,"Section,Scientific,Revolution"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Changing Views of the Universe,"Changing,Views,Universe"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Until the mid - 1500s, Europeans believed in the Earth - centered universe theory of Ptolemy and Aristotle, which was supported by the Church.","mid,Europeans,believed,Earth,centered,universe,theory,Ptolemy,Aristotle,supported,Church"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1543, Nicolaus Copernicus published On the Revolutions of the Heavenly Spheres. Proposed a heliocentric (sun - centered) model of the universe.","Nicolaus,Copernicus,published,Revolutions,Heavenly,Spheres,Proposed,heliocentric,sun,centered,model,universe"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Most experts rejected Copernicus's theory. It challenged classical and religious teachings.,"experts,rejected,Copernicus,theory,challenged,classical,religious,teachings"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Tycho Brahe set up an observatory. His observations provided evidence for Copernicus's theory.,"Tycho,Brahe,set,observatory,observations,provided,evidence,Copernicus,theory"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Johannes Kepler used Brahe's data. Calculated that planets move in elliptical orbits, supporting Copernicus's heliocentric view.","Johannes,Kepler,used,Brahe,data,Calculated,planets,move,elliptical,orbits,supporting,Copernicus,heliocentric,view"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Galileo Galilei built a telescope. Observed Jupiter's moons, which supported the heliocentric view. His discoveries were opposed by scholars and condemned by the Church. He was tried and placed under house arrest.","Galileo,Galilei,built,telescope,Observed,Jupiter,moons,supported,heliocentric,view,discoveries,opposed,scholars,condemned,Church,tried,placed,house,arrest"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,A New Scientific Method,"New,Scientific,Method"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In the early 1600s, a new scientific method emerged. Based on observation and experimentation.","early,new,scientific,method,emerged,Based,observation,experimentation"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Francis Bacon stressed experimentation and observation. Wanted science to improve people's lives through practical technologies.,"Francis,Bacon,stressed,experimentation,observation,Wanted,science,improve,people,lives,practical,technologies"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"René Descartes emphasized human reasoning. His famous statement was ""I think, therefore I am.""","Ren,Descartes,emphasized,human,reasoning,famous,statement,think,therefore"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The scientific method involved collecting and measuring data. Proposing a hypothesis, testing it, and repeating the process.","scientific,method,involved,collecting,measuring,data,Proposing,hypothesis,testing,repeating,process"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Breakthroughs in Medicine and Chemistry,"Breakthroughs,Medicine,Chemistry"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In medicine, Andreas Vesalius published On the Structure of the Human Body in 1543. It was the first accurate study of human anatomy.","medicine,Andreas,Vesalius,published,Structure,Human,Body,first,accurate,study,human,anatomy"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Ambroise Paré developed new surgical techniques and an anti - infection ointment.,"Ambroise,Par,developed,new,surgical,techniques,anti,infection,ointment"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,William Harvey described blood circulation in the early 1600s.,"William,Harvey,described,blood,circulation,early"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Anton van Leeuwenhoek perfected the microscope. First to see cells and microorganisms.,"Anton,van,Leeuwenhoek,perfected,microscope,First,see,cells,microorganisms"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In chemistry, alchemy was transformed. Robert Boyle refined the view of chemicals. Distinguished between elements and compounds, and explained the behavior of gases.","chemistry,alchemy,transformed,Robert,Boyle,refined,view,chemicals,Distinguished,elements,compounds,explained,behavior,gases"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Isaac Newton Links the Sciences,"Isaac,Newton,Links,Sciences"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Isaac Newton saw an apple fall. Wondered if the same force controlled the planets' movement.,"Isaac,Newton,saw,apple,fall,Wondered,force,controlled,planets,movement"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,He developed the theory of gravity. Showed that a single force keeps planets in orbit.,"developed,theory,gravity,Showed,single,force,keeps,planets,orbit"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1687, Newton published a book explaining the law of gravity. Argued nature follows uniform laws.","Newton,published,book,explaining,law,gravity,Argued,nature,follows,uniform,laws"
7 IDX G9 HIST S.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Newton's laws held for over 200 years. Calculus, developed in part by Newton, is still used today.","Newton,laws,held,years,Calculus,developed,part,Newton,still,used,today"
