8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Copernicus Challenges Ancient Astronomy,"Copernicus,Challenges,Ancient,Astronomy"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1543, Polish scholar Nicolaus Copernicus proposed heliocentric. (Sun centered)","Polish,scholar,Nicolaus,Copernicus,proposed,heliocentric,Sun,centered"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Earth is one of the planets that surround the Sun.,"Earth,one,planets,surround,Sun"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Experts rejected this theory, since people during that time were still believing the medieval teachings, including religious concepts.","Experts,rejected,theory,since,people,time,still,believing,medieval,teachings,including,religious,concepts"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In late 1500s, the Danish astronomer Tycho Brahe provided evidence to support Copernicus’ heliocentric theory by accumulating observation results.","late,Danish,astronomer,Tycho,Brahe,provided,evidence,support,Copernicus,heliocentric,theory,accumulating,observation,results"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The assistant of Brahe, Johannes Kepler used Brahe’s data to calculate the orbit of planets orbiting the sun in support of heliocentric. He also shown that the planets orbit the sun in ellipses.","assistant,Brahe,Johannes,Kepler,used,Brahe,data,calculate,orbit,planets,orbiting,sun,support,heliocentric,also,shown,planets,orbit,sun,ellipses"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Galileo’s “Heresies”,"Galileo,Heresies"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Galileo assembled an astronomical telescope that observed four moons moving around Jupiter. He publicly stated that Copernicus’ view was correct.,"Galileo,assembled,astronomical,telescope,observed,four,moons,moving,around,Jupiter,publicly,stated,Copernicus,view,correct"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"This caused an uproar in society. Other scholars attacked Galileo, and the church condemned him for challenging the religious teachings.","caused,uproar,society,scholars,attacked,Galileo,church,condemned,challenging,religious,teachings"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1633, Galileo was tried before the Inquisition, and for a year after- ward he was kept under house arrest. Threatened with death unless he withdrew his “heresies,” Galileo agreed to state publicly in court that Earth stands motionless at the center of the universe.","Galileo,tried,Inquisition,year,ward,kept,house,arrest,Threatened,death,unless,withdrew,heresies,Galileo,agreed,state,publicly,court,Earth,stands,motionless,center,universe"
