8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,14.1 The Search for Spices,"Search,Spices"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Motivation for Exploring the Seas,"Motivation,Exploring,Seas"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Europeans traded with Asians long time ago.,"Europeans,traded,Asians,long,time,ago"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Crusades introduced luxury goods to Europe from Asia.,"Crusades,introduced,luxury,goods,Europe,Asia"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Most valued item during their trade was the spices.,"valued,item,trade,spices"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Chief source of spices was Moluccas.,"Chief,source,spices,Moluccas"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Most goods from Asia were brought to Europe by Italian traders. They carried the goods from East Mediterranean which had goods previously dropped by the Muslim traders.,"goods,Asia,brought,Europe,Italian,traders,carried,goods,East,Mediterranean,goods,previously,dropped,Muslim,traders"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Other Europeans realized that having direct access to Asia would reduce a large amount of cost which they had previously spent on the Italian traders.,"Europeans,realized,direct,access,Asia,would,reduce,large,amount,cost,previously,spent,Italian,traders"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Portugal Sails East,"Portugal,Sails,East"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Prince Henry sponsored the Portugal explorations.,"Prince,Henry,sponsored,Portugal,explorations"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Mapping the African Coast,"Mapping,African,Coast"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Prince Henry seized the chance of converting African, who originally believed in Islam or tribal religions, to Christians.","Prince,Henry,seized,chance,converting,African,originally,believed,Islam,tribal,religions,Christians"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Prince Henry also wanted to reach Asia in an easier way, with going around the Southern tip of Africa.","Prince,Henry,also,wanted,reach,Asia,easier,way,going,around,Southern,tip,Africa"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Cartographers – map makers,"Cartographers,map,makers"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Seeking India,"Seeking,India"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1497, Vasco da Gama led the troupes around the Southern tip of Africa (Cape of Good Hope)","Vasco,da,Gama,led,troupes,around,Southern,tip,Africa,Cape,Good,Hope"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Da Gama eventually reached port of Calicut, on the west coast of India.","Da,Gama,eventually,reached,port,Calicut,west,coast,India"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Da Gama made large profit out of the spices, and dominated main ports on the coast of India.","Da,Gama,made,large,profit,spices,dominated,main,ports,coast,India"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Columbus Sails West,"Columbus,Sails,West"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Italian navigator named Christopher Columbus wanted to reach East India, so he voyaged from Europe to the West.","Italian,navigator,named,Christopher,Columbus,wanted,reach,East,India,voyaged,Europe,West"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Reaching Faraway Lands,"Reaching,Faraway,Lands"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Columbus persuaded Ferdinand and Isabella of Spain to sponsor him.,"Columbus,persuaded,Ferdinand,Isabella,Spain,sponsor"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"On August 3, 1492, Columbus set sail to the west in three small ships.","August,Columbus,set,sail,west,three,small,ships"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"On October 12, a land came in sight.","October,land,came,sight"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"He assumed that he encountered the Indies, so he called the people Indians.","assumed,encountered,Indies,called,people,Indians"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Dividing the Globe in Half,"Dividing,Globe,Half"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1493 Pope Alexander VI set a Line of Demarcation, dividing the non-European world into two zones. Spain has the right to trade and explore on the west side, while Portugal has the right to trade and explore on the east side.","Pope,Alexander,VI,set,Line,Demarcation,dividing,non,European,world,two,zones,Spain,right,trade,explore,west,side,Portugal,right,trade,explore,east,side"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"The terms of the Line were agreed to in the Treaty of Tordesillas, signed between two countries in 1494.","terms,Line,agreed,Treaty,Tordesillas,signed,two,countries"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Naming the Western Hemisphere,"Naming,Western,Hemisphere"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In 1507, a German cartographer named the Brazil region as “America”.","German,cartographer,named,Brazil,region,America"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The islands Columbus had explored in the Caribbean had been known as the West Indies.,"islands,Columbus,explored,Caribbean,known,West,Indies"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The Search for a Direct Route Continues,"Search,Direct,Route,Continues"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"On September 20, 1519, a Portuguese nobleman named Ferdinand Magellan set out for finding a way to the Pacific with five ships. At last, he reached the coast of South America.","September,Portuguese,nobleman,named,Ferdinand,Magellan,set,finding,way,Pacific,five,ships,last,reached,coast,South,America"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"In November 1520, Magellan and his crew entered a bay, and found a strait leading to the Pacific, would later be known as the Magellan Strait.","November,Magellan,crew,entered,bay,found,strait,leading,Pacific,would,later,known,Magellan,Strait"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"They sailed for nearly four months, then reached the Philippines, where Magellan was killed.","sailed,nearly,four,months,reached,Philippines,Magellan,killed"
8 IDX HIST S+.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"After setting out from Portugal for three years, the remaining survivors came back to Spain. Magellan’s expedition is considered the first to circumnavigate the Earth, even though Magellan himself did not survive the journey.","setting,Portugal,three,years,remaining,survivors,came,back,Spain,Magellan,expedition,considered,first,circumnavigate,Earth,even,though,Magellan,survive,journey"
