S2 FINALS IDX G9 PHY S.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,• Work (W):  Transfer of energy when a force moves an object.,"Work,W,Transfer,energy,force,moves,object"
S2 FINALS IDX G9 PHY S.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"• If force and motion are in the same direction, work is positive (energy increases).","force,motion,direction,work,positive,energy,increases"
S2 FINALS IDX G9 PHY S.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"• If force opposes motion (e.g braking), work is negative (energy decreases).","force,opposes,motion,e,g,braking,work,negative,energy,decreases"
S2 FINALS IDX G9 PHY S.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"• If force is perpendicular to motion (e.g., circular motion), no work is done.","force,perpendicular,motion,e,g,circular,motion,work,done"
S2 FINALS IDX G9 PHY S.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,• Work -Energy Theorem:,"Work,Energy,Theorem"
S2 FINALS IDX G9 PHY S.pdf,2025-06-27 02:49:14,• The work done on an object equals its change in kinetic energy.,"work,done,object,equals,change,kinetic,energy"
