1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,-Intersection ⋂: A ∩ B is the set containing elements common to both set A and 	 set B. Also written in the form,"Intersection,B,set,containing,elements,common,set,set,B,Also,written,form"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,-Union ⋃: A ∪ B is the set containing all elements of A and B.,"Union,B,set,containing,elements,B"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,-Difference -: A - B is the set containing elements that are in A but not in B.,"Difference,B,set,containing,elements,B"
