1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-Element (∈): If set A contains a certain element, it is symbolized as x ∈ A. It 	 reads x is an element of A.","Element,set,contains,certain,element,symbolized,x,reads,x,element"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-Not an Element (∉): If set A does not contain a certain element, it is symbolized 	as x ∉ A. It reads x is not an element of A.","Element,set,contain,certain,element,symbolized,x,reads,x,element"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-Subset (⊂ or ⊆): A set A is a subset of set B if every element of A is also an 	element of B. It is symbolized as A ⊂ B or A ⊆ B. A ⊂ B means A is a proper 	subset of B (B has elements not in A), while A ⊆ B can also mean A equals B.","Subset,set,subset,set,B,every,element,also,element,B,symbolized,B,B,B,means,proper,subset,B,B,elements,B,also,mean,equals,B"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,-Superset (⊃ or ⊇): A set B is a superset of set A if every element of A is also an 	element of B. It is represented as B ⊃ A or B ⊇ A. This can be understood as the 	opposite of a subset in which the second set is a subset of the first set and not 	the other way around.,"Superset,set,B,superset,set,every,element,also,element,B,represented,B,B,understood,opposite,subset,second,set,subset,first,set,way,around"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,-Intersection (⋂): A ∩ B is the set containing elements common to both set A 	and B.,"Intersection,B,set,containing,elements,common,set,B"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-Union (⋃): A ∪ B is the set containing all elements in either A, B, or both.","Union,B,set,containing,elements,either,B"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-Complement ('): The complement of set A, denoted by A', is the set of elements 	in the universal set that are not in A. (In textbooks its also denoted as a bar on 	top of the name of the set, but it couldn’t be entered on a computer so I went 	with the other representation.)","Complement,complement,set,denoted,set,elements,universal,set,textbooks,also,denoted,bar,top,name,set,entered,computer,went,representation"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-Difference (-): The difference of set A and B, denoted by A - B, is the set of all 	elements which are in A but not in B. This could also be achieved through 	operations: For a set C C=A-B when for every n∈C, n∈A, n∉B or","Difference,difference,set,B,denoted,B,set,elements,B,could,also,achieved,operations,set,C,C,B,every,n,C,n,n,B"
1 G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"C={n丨n∈A, n∉B}","C,n,丨,n,A,n,B"
