5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Transformation:,Transformation
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"a transformation of a geometric figure is a change in its position, shape, or size.","transformation,geometric,figure,change,position,shape,size"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,The original figure is the preimage. The resulting figure is an image.(the preimage and image must be similar),"original,figure,preimage,resulting,figure,image,preimage,image,must,similar"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,An isometry is a transformation in which the preimage and image are congruent,"isometry,transformation,preimage,image,congruent"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,A transformation maps a figure onto its image and may be described with arrow(--->)notation. Prime (')notation is sometimes used to identify image points,"transformation,maps,figure,onto,image,may,described,arrow,notation,Prime,notation,sometimes,used,identify,image,points"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"Notice that you list corresponding points of the preimage and image in the sameorder, as youvdo for corresponding points of congruent or similar figures.","Notice,list,corresponding,points,preimage,image,sameorder,youvdo,corresponding,points,congruent,similar,figures"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Translation:,Translation
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,a translation(or slide) is an isometry that maps all points of a figure the same distance in the same direction.,"translation,slide,isometry,maps,points,figure,distance,direction"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"A composition of translation is a combination of two or more transformations. In composition, each transformation is performed on the image of the preceding transformation","composition,translation,combination,two,transformations,composition,transformation,performed,image,preceding,transformation"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Reflection:,Reflection
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"A reflection (or fip) is an isometry in which a figure and its image have opposite orientations. Thus, a reflected image in a mirror appears “backwards.”","reflection,fip,isometry,figure,image,opposite,orientations,Thus,reflected,image,mirror,appears,backwards"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,You can use the following two rules to reflect a figure across a line r.,"use,following,two,rules,reflect,figure,across,line,r"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-If a point A is on line r, then the image of A is A itself (that is,A'=A)","point,line,r,image"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-If a point B is not on line r, then r is the perpendicular bisector of BB'","point,B,line,r,r,perpendicular,bisector,BB"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Rotation:,Rotation
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"To describe a rotation , you need to know the center of rotation (a point), the angle of rotation (a positive number of degrees)and whether the rotation is clockwise or counterclockwise.Unless stated otherwise.rotations in this book are counterclockwise.","describe,rotation,need,know,center,rotation,point,angle,rotation,positive,number,degrees,whether,rotation,clockwise,counterclockwise,Unless,stated,otherwise,rotations,book,counterclockwise"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,You can use the following two rules to rotate a figure through x° about a point R:,"use,following,two,rules,rotate,figure,x,point,R"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-The image of R is itself (that is,R'= R)","image,R,R,R"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"-For any point V,Rv'= RV and m/VRV'= x.","point,V,Rv,RV,VRV,x"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,A regular polygon has a center that is equidistant from its vertices. Segments that connect the center to the vertices divide the polygon into congruent triangles. You can use this fact to find rotation images of regular polygons.,"regular,polygon,center,equidistant,vertices,Segments,connect,center,vertices,divide,polygon,congruent,triangles,use,fact,find,rotation,images,regular,polygons"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Composition of Reflections:,"Composition,Reflections"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,Glide Reflections:,"Glide,Reflections"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,"If two figures are congruent and have opposite orientations (but are not simply reflections of each other), then there is a slide and a reflection that will map one onto the other.","two,figures,congruent,opposite,orientations,simply,reflections,slide,reflection,map,one,onto"
5 IDX G9 MATH H.docx,2025-06-27 02:49:14,A glide reflection is the composition of a glide (translation) and areflection across a line parallel to the direction of translation.,"glide,reflection,composition,glide,translation,areflection,across,line,parallel,direction,translation"
